for a necessary market-rate MD salary and maintenance capex.","The asset-based floor (£1.2m) is very close to the conservative enterprise value, providing high downside protection.","The 100% concentration in 5 blue-chip energy clients is the defining risk factor for any acquirer.","Strong cash position and low gearing make the business highly attractive for a leveraged buyout."],"red_flags":["Extreme customer concentration: 100% of debtors in 5 accounts.","Linear scaling: Headcount and revenue growth are perfectly correlated, indicating no economies of scale.","Sector risk: 100% exposure to the Oil & Gas technical services cycle."],"narrative":"Macinnes Tooling is a 'textbook' stable engineering firm. Its valuation is bolstered by a 5-year track record of 3.3% growth and rock-solid 40% margins. While the sector expert suggests multiples as low as 1.5x for micro-entities, Macinnes's blue-chip client list and modern CNC asset base justify a premium multiple of 2.75x on adjusted EBITDA. The resulting Equity Value of ~£1.45m is well-supported by a strong Net Asset Value of £1.2m. The primary hurdle for a transaction will be the 'Critical' customer concentration; a buyer will likely require an earn-out structure or significant indemnities regarding the retention of the top 5 energy sector contracts."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Macinnes Tooling","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":65,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Heavy earnout and retention to mitigate 100% customer concentration risk.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly risk-averse regarding the Oil & Gas sector and the stability of the top 5 clients.","consideration":{"total_headline":1450000,"upfront_cash":725000,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":225000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 12 and month 24 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":500000,"earnout_metric":"Customer Retention & EBITDA Floor","earnout_period_months