 cycle is lengthening, with stock and debtor days increasing as a percentage of revenue."],"narrative":"Cordell Engineering is a high-margin, debt-free micro-SME that presents a classic 'lifestyle' business profile. While the underlying profitability is excellent (Adjusted EBITDA of £371.5k), the valuation is constrained by the company's small scale and the inherent risks of owner-dependency and revenue volatility. The base Enterprise Value of £836k reflects a 2.25x multiple, which is fair for a technical service firm of this size. The final Equity Value of £1.1M is bolstered significantly by the company's 'clean' balance sheet and high cash reserves. However, a buyer must be wary of the aging asset base and the recent aggressive capital extraction by the current owners. A deal structure involving a significant upfront payment for the net assets plus an earn-out based on maintaining the 2025 revenue levels would be the most prudent approach."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Cordell Engineering","analysis_date":"2025-05-24","score":65,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-heavy protection with high earnout weighting to mitigate revenue volatility and owner dependency.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 21% revenue drop in 2024 and the 'capex cliff' regarding plant and machinery.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":550000,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":200000,"deferred_schedule":"Two equal installments of £100k at 12 and 24 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":350000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Floor & Revenue Stability","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Revenue Volatility (21% drop in 2024) and Owner Dependency. Earnout ensures the business maintains a normalized EBITDA of £371k without the current directors' personal involvement.","retention_escrow":110000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months pending no warranty claims related to tax or undisclosed liabilities."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Engineering and technical services within a 50-mile radius; no solicitation of existing clients or staff.","consultancy_arrangement":"Directors retained on a part-time consultancy basis for months 7-12 at a fixed day rate."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for immediate replacement of fully depreciated Plant & Machinery","Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from aggressive dividend extraction in 2024","Indemnity for potential bad debt on trade debtors over 90 days"],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":217698,"rationale":"Due to the lengthening cash conversion cycle and recent inventory spikes, completion accounts are necessary to ensure the buyer does not inherit a working capital deficit."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1100000,"expected_case":925000,"worst_case":550000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"Standard SME structure with a mix of upfront cash and performance-linked deferred payments.","suitable_when":"Due diligence confirms the 2025 recovery is sustainable and the customer base is diversified.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":770000,"upfront_percent":70,"deferred":165000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in full at 12 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":165000,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Revenue Volatility. Specifically tied to maintaining revenue at or above £1.3M to prove the 2024 dip was an anomaly.","retention_escrow":55000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon finalization of first-year statutory accounts."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in technical engineering ser