commended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The Conservative structure is recommended due to the combination of high owner dependency, significant revenue volatility (21% drop), and the 'capex cliff' identified by the operational expert. The business is currently being managed for personal wealth extraction (pensions/dividends), and an earnout is essential to ensure the EBITDA remains sustainable once the owners exit and professional management is installed.","negotiation_priorities":["Normalization of working capital to account for the recent inventory spike.","Securing a long handover period to mitigate key person risk.","Price adjustment or indemnity for the fully depreciated plant and machinery.","Verification of the 'Other Creditors' balance of £123k."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Further dividend extraction prior to completion.","Refusal of key directors to sign a 24-month non-compete.","Discovery of significant undisclosed maintenance requirements for the vehicle fleet."],"key_findings":["The business has excellent liquidity (£307k cash) which should be used to fund the upfront portion of the deal.","Revenue is project-heavy (72% installation), making an earnout based on revenue stability a logical requirement.","The gap between seller expectations (£1.8M+) and fair value (£1.1M) is the primary hurdle; the earnout is the only tool to bridge this."],"narrative":"Cordell Engineering is a classic 'lifestyle' business that is financially healthy but operationally stagnant. The deal structure must balance the high cash reserves and profitability against the risks of a shrinking asset base and volatile revenue. A Conservative structure protects the buyer from the 'harvest' mentality of the current owners, ensuring that the price paid is reflective of future performance rather than historical peaks. By tying a significant portion of the consideration to a 24-month earnout, the buyer mitigates the risk of the business declining once the owners' personal relationships are removed from the sales cycle."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Cordell Engineering","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":72,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2022":{"revenue":1332473,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":695539,"gross_profit":636934,"gross_margin_percent":47.8,"administrative_expenses":525317,"operating_profit":111617,"operating_margin_percent":8.38,"depreciation_amortisation":26897,"ebitda":138514,"interest_payable":1319,"interest_coverage_ratio":84.62,"profit_before_tax":110405,"corporation_tax":19209,"effective_tax_rate_percent":17.4,"net_profit":91196,"net_margin_percent":6.84},"2023":{"revenue":1598800,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":19.99,"cost_of_sales":816112,"gross_profit":782688,"gross_margin_percent":48.95,"administrative_expenses":429450,"operating_profit":353238,"operating_margin_percent":22.09,"depreciation_amortisation":28120,"ebitda":381358,"interest_payable":959,"interest_coverage_ratio":368.34,"profit_before_tax":354021,"corporation_tax":83882,"effective_tax_rate_percent":23.7,"net_profit":270139,"net_margin_percent":16.9},"2024":{"revenue":1258568,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-21.28,"cost_of_sales":635133,"gross_profit":623435,"gross_margin_percent":49.54,"administrative_expenses":421664,"operating_profit":201771,"operating_margin_percent":16.03,"depreciation_amortisation":35386,"ebitda":237157,"interest_payable":94,"interest_coverage_ratio":2146.5,"profit_before_tax":209800,"corporation_tax":50708,"effective_tax_rate_percent":24.17,"net_profit":159092,"net_margin_percent":12.64},"2025":{"revenue":1310453,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":4.12,"cost_of_sales":676756,"gross_profit":633697,"gross_margin_percent":48.36,"administrative_expenses":380548,"operating_profit":253149,"operating_margin_percent":19.32,"depreciation_amortisation":37852,"ebitda":291001,"interest_payable":0,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":257309,"corporation_tax":51393,"effective_tax_rate_percent