onsistent 3.3-3.4% YoY increase over five years.","Gross margins are perfectly flat at 40.0%, indicating strong pricing power and effective direct cost control.","Operating margins are highly consistent at 10%, suggesting that overheads are managed strictly in line with revenue growth.","Staff costs are the primary overhead driver, representing approximately 42% of total revenue.","The company has successfully deleveraged, with interest payable falling from 28k to 17k while coverage improved to 21.8x.","EBITDA has grown steadily from 470k to 536k, providing a reliable basis for valuation.","The effective tax rate is consistent at 19%, suggesting no complex tax structures or significant deferred tax volatility.","Net assets have grown by over 40% since 2020, entirely through retained earnings."],"red_flags":["High customer concentration: Top 5 debtors account for 100% of the outstanding sales ledger balance.","Staff costs exceed total administrative expenses in the breakdown, suggesting some staff costs may be capitalized or allocated to Cost of Sales, requiring further audit."],"narrative":"Macinnes Tooling presents a profile of exceptional financial stability and predictability. Over the five-year period analyzed, the company has demonstrated a remarkably consistent revenue CAGR of 3.36%, with gross and operating margins remaining virtually unchanged. This suggests a mature business with highly disciplined cost management and a stable market position within the Engineering & Technical Services sector. Profitability is of high quality, with net profit closely tracking operating performance and no evidence of exceptional or one-off items distorting the figures. The cost structure is predominantly fixed, driven by a skilled workforce of 32 employees, yet the business has successfully maintained its 10% operating margin despite inflationary pressures. From a debt service perspective, the company is in a very strong position; the interest coverage ratio has nearly doubled since 2020, and the gearing ratio has fallen significantly. This provides a robust platform for a leveraged buyout or further expansion. The primary financial risk identified is the extreme concentration in the sales ledger, where five blue-chip energy sector clients represent the entirety of the trade debt. While these are high-quality debtors, the loss of any single account would have a material impact on cash flow. Overall, the financial performance is indicative of a well-run, low-risk enterprise with reliable earnings."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":9,"financialPeriodId":10,"targetCompanyId":7,"intangibleAssets":"0","tangibleFixedAssets":"1595000","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"505000","tradeDebtors":"638000","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":"427000","totalCurrentAssets":"1570000","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"735000","totalCurrentLiabilities":"735000","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":"329000","totalLongTermLiabilities":"329000","shareCapital":"100000","retainedEarnings":"2001000","totalEquity":"2101000","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":13,"createdAt":"2026-03-18T03:09:39.539Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-18T03:09:39.539Z"},"fixedAssets":{"id":2,"targetCompanyId":7,"reportDate":"2024-01-31","totalGrossBookValue":"2368500","totalAccumulatedDepreciation":"1159600","totalNetBookValue":"1208900","propertyGrossValue":"125000","propertyNetBookValue":"81250","plantMachineryGrossValue":"1048000","plantMachineryNetBookValue":"508100","vehi