ing management team (Project Managers) reduces the MD's workload."},{"item":"Bad Debt Provisioning (Aged Debtors)","category":"bad_debt_provision","amount":19300,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2024,"justification":"26.3% of the ledger (£193,000) is aged 31-60 days. While no debt is >90 days, a conservative 10% provision on the aged portion is prudent given high customer concentration.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":7,"case_for_inclusion":"High customer concentration (71% in top 3) means any friction with a single blue-chip client creates significant cash flow and earnings risk.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller will argue that the debtors are blue-chip entities (Redrow, Countryside) with zero historical default and that payment timing is purely contractual."},{"item":"Deferred Maintenance - Workshop & Tools","category":"deferred_maintenance","amount":15000,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2024,"justification":"Operational expert identified workshop tools and equipment (£45k cost) with a low NBV of £9,000, indicating they are nearing the end of their useful life and require a higher maintenance/replacement budget.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":6,"case_for_inclusion":"The low net book value of core workshop assets suggests an imminent requirement for capital outlay or increased repair costs to maintain productivity.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue that recent aggressive vehicle fleet renewal proves they reinvest sufficiently and that tools are replaced via Opex as needed."}],"total_add_backs":352800,"total_deductions":43800,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":678400,"base":678400,"optimistic":1031200},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":722200,"plus_add_backs":0,"minus_deductions":43800,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":678400},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Owner-Director","current_salary":68000,"estimated_market_rate":77500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M: Working MD/Owner-Director (£45,000–£70,000) - adjusted to high end due to revenue being at the top of the bracket (£4.18M).","adjustment":9500,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Retention of the top 3 property group clients (Langtree, Redrow, Countryside).","Maintenance of the 50% gross margin through continued pricing discipline.","Ability to recruit skilled trades (Electricians/Plumbers) to support the 22.6% CAGR."],"sensitivity_factors":["Customer concentration: Loss of one top-tier client would impact EBITDA by ~20-25%.","Labor costs: Wage inflation for technical trades in the UK SME sector."],"upside_scenarios":["Utilizing the £588k cash reserve for bolt-on acquisitions.","Leveraging the clean balance sheet to secure lower-cost financing for further fleet expansion."],"downside_scenarios":["A downturn in the UK residential construction sector affecting the primary debtor group.","Increased debtor days leading to working capital friction."]},"key_findings":["Exceptional gross margin stability at 50% over 4 years indicates strong niche positioning.","Negative cash conversion cycle allows the business to fund rapid growth through trade credit rather than debt.","The business is 'clean' with very few personal expenses or related-party distortions.","Operational gearing is evident: Operating profit is growing significantly faster than revenue."],"red_flags":["Extreme customer concentration: 71.4% of debtors tied to 3 entities.","Aging of sales ledger: 26.3% of debt is over 30 days, which may indicate 'pay-when-paid' dynamics from large contractors."],"narrative":"Adam & Co is a high-quality acquisition target with robust and transparent earnings. The reported EBITDA of £722k is largely sustainable, with the primary adjustments being a minor market-rate salary correction for the director and a prudent provision for aged debtors. The quality of earnings is bolstered by the fact that the business has successfully scaled revenue at a 22.6% CAGR while actually expanding its operating margins. The lack of owner-dependency (evidenced by a full management/PM layer) and the modern state of the vehicle fleet make the earnings highly transferable to a new owner. The main risk for a buyer is the concentration of revenue within a few large property groups, which should be addressed through a robust earn-out structure or commercial due diligence on those specific contracts."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Adam & Co","analysis_date":"2025-05-25","score":85,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":678400,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2.5,"multiple_justification":"A multiple of 2.5x is selected, which is above the sector midpoint but within the sub-£5M revenue guardrails. This reflects exceptional growth (22.6% CAGR) and margin stability (50% Gross Margin), offset by critical customer concentration.","premium_factors_applied":["Consistent double-digit revenue growth (22.6% CAGR)","Expanding operating margins (12% to 16%)","Modern asset base with 50% of fleet replaced in last 24 months","Negative cash conversion cycle funding growth via trade credit"],"discount_factors_applied":["Critical customer concentration (Top 3 = 71.4% of revenue)","Micro-cap size (Revenue < £5M) limiting buyer pool","Sector cyclicality (Exposure to UK residential construction)"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":1017600,"base":1696000,"optimistic":2035200}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":1696000,"plus_cash":588000,"minus_long_term_debt":17000,"minus_director_loans":0,"minus_bad_debt_provision":19300,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":0,"other_adjustments":[{"description":"Deferred Maintenance Adjustment","amount":15000}],"equity_value":{"conservative":1554300,"base":2232700,"optimistic":2571900}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":1490000,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":-19300,"adjusted_nav":1470700,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":4180000,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.4,"high":0.6},"implied_ev_range":{"low":1672000,"high":2508000}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":1554300,"equity_value_mid":2232700,"equity_value_high":2571900},"primary_methodology":"ebitda_multiple","cross_check_alignment":"strong"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":1865600,"equity_value":2402300},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":1526400,"equity_value":2063100},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":2035200,"equity_value":2571900},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":1356800,"equity_value":1893500},"key_customer_loss_impact":424000,"director_replacement_impact":23750},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":3000000,"high":4500000},"seller_anchor_points":["Emotional value of building a 38-staff operation","High cash balance of £588k viewed as 'extra' rather than part of EV","Strong 20%+ growth trajectory used to justify forward-looking multiples"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. The seller is likely to anchor on a 4x-5x multiple of reported EBITDA or a percentage of turnover. A bridge will be required via an earn-out to mitigate the customer concentration risk."},"key_findings":["The business is exceptionally clean with high-quality earnings and a strong balance sheet.","Operational gearing is high, with profit growing at 1.4x the rate of revenue.","The negative cash conversion cycle is a major value driver, allowing growth without external debt.","Valuation is heavily supported by a high Net Asset Value floor of £1.47M."],"red_flags":["Critical dependency on 5 customers; loss of Langtree Group (31%) would impair value significantly.","Sales ledger aging (26% > 30 days) suggests potential working capital friction with blue-chip contractors.","Sector risk: High exposure to UK residential construction cycles."],"narrative":"Adam & Co is a high-performing SME that justifies a premium within its size bracket due to its 22.6% CAGR and 50% stable gross margins. While the sector expert suggests a 1.5x-3.0x EBITDA range for this size, the company's modern fleet and lack of owner-dependency push it toward the higher end (2.5x). The primary valuation challenge is the extreme customer concentration, which creates a binary risk profile. A fair equity value of £2.23M is proposed, which includes the benefit of the £588k cash reserve. Buyers should structure the deal with a significant earn-out component (30-40%) tied to the retention of the top 3 clients to bridge the gap between the calculated fair value and likely higher seller expectations."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Adam & Co","analysis_date":"2025-05-25","score":72,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Minimize upfront risk by tying the majority of the value to the retention of the top 3 customers and the owner's successful transition.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 71.4% customer concentration and the potential for a 'binary' loss of the Langtree Group contract.","consideration":{"total_headline":2232700,"upfront_cash":1116350,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":223270,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 6 and month 12 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":893080,"earnout_metric":"Customer Retention & EBITDA Floor","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"40% of the deal is contingent on the top 3 clients (Langtree, Redrow, Countryside) maintaining at least 90% of their 2024 revenue levels.","retention_escrow":223270,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months pending no warranty claims related to undisclosed liabilities or tax."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":24,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in UK residential construction electrical/plumbing services.","consultancy_arrangement":"Part-time consultancy for year 2 to ensure relationship transfer to new MD."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Specific indemnity for any bad debt write-offs exceeding £19,300 in the first 12 months.","Indemnity against loss of Langtree Group contract within 6 months of completion."],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":658000,"rationale":"Ensures the high cash balance (£588k) is verified and working capital is sufficient to fund the negative cash cycle."},"effective_price":{"best_case":2232700,"expected_case":1897795,"worst_case":1116350}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"A middle-ground approach that rewards the seller for growth while protecting the buyer against immediate client churn.","suitable_when":"Due diligence confirms stable relationships with the top 5 clients and the management layer is proven to be autonomous.","consideration":{"total_headline":2350000,"upfront_cash":1645000,"upfront_percent":70,"deferred":235000,"deferred_schedule":"12 months post-completion, subject to standard set-off rights.","earnout_maximum":470000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Growth","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Tied to achieving an Adjusted EBITDA of £700k+, validating the 22.6% CAGR trajectory.","retention_escrow":117500,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon finalization of first-year statutory accounts."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Restricted from soliciting top 5 clients or key project managers.","consultancy_arrangement":"Retained on a day-rate basis for strategic tenders only."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for any historical tax liabilities related to the 2023-2024 fleet renewal program."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":18,"de_minimis":7500,"basket":35000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":658000,"rationale":"The business is 'clean' and stable; a locked box simplifies the closing process for a high-performing target."},"effective_price":{"best_case":2350000,"expected_case":2115000,"worst_case":1527500}},{"name":"Competitive","strategy":"Aggressive upfront offer to bridge the gap with seller expectations, relying on the high NAV floor for downside protection.","suitable_when":"Multiple bidders are involved and the buyer intends to use the £588k cash for immediate bolt-on acquisitions.","consideration":{"total_headline":2600000,"upfront_cash":2210000,"upfront_percent":85,"deferred":390000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid at 6 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"N/A","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"No earnout used to make the offer more attractive than competitors; risk managed via higher warranties.","retention_escrow":0,"escrow_release_conditions":"N/A"},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Standard industry non-compete.","consultancy_arrangement":"None; reliance on the existing 3 Project Managers."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Full indemnity for any loss of the top 2 customers within the first 12 months (clawback provision)."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":50000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":658000,"rationale":"Speed of execution is the priority in a competitive bid."},"effective_price":{"best_case":2600000,"expected_case":2600000,"worst_case":2210000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"Despite the company's high quality, the 71.4% concentration in just three customers (all in the cyclical construction sector) represents a binary risk that cannot be ignored. A structure that places 40-50% of the value at risk via an earnout tied to client retention is the only way to bridge the gap between the £2.23M valuation and the seller's likely £3M+ expectation without exposing the buyer to catastrophic loss if a single contract is terminated.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the 'Exceptional Distribution Costs' (£352k) to ensure they are truly non-recurring.","Securing long-term commitment or non-solicitation agreements from the 3 Project Managers.","Confirming the contractual 'notice periods' for the Langtree Group and Redrow contracts.","Negotiating the treatment of the £588k cash (Seller views as 'extra', Buyer views as necessary for the negative cash cycle)."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Loss of Langtree Group contract prior to completion.","Discovery that the negative cash conversion cycle is dependent on 'pay-when-paid' clauses that are legally unenforceable.","Refusal of the owner to provide a 24-month non-compete."],"key_findings":["The business is exceptionally clean with a high NAV floor (£1.47M) providing good downside protection.","Operational gearing is strong, but customer concentration is the 'Achilles heel'.","The negative cash conversion cycle is a major asset but requires careful working capital pegging.","The modern fleet significantly reduces the risk of hidden capex requirements post-acquisition."],"narrative":"Adam & Co is a 'gem' SME with professionalized operations and high margins. However, the valuation gap is significant because the seller likely values the business on its growth trajectory, while a prudent buyer must value it on its risk-adjusted stability. The Conservative structure is recommended to protect against the cyclicality of the UK construction sector and the extreme reliance on five customers. By using a heavy earnout, the buyer can offer a higher headline price to satisfy the seller's ego while only paying that premium if the revenue (and the key relationships) actually transfer."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Adam & Co","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":92,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2020":{"rev