ional leverage as the business scales.","Staff costs are the primary overhead driver, representing 40% of revenue, yet they are being managed efficiently relative to growth.","Interest coverage has improved from 18.5x to 159.1x, reflecting a de-risked balance sheet and high debt serviceability.","Net profit tracks operating profit closely, suggesting high earnings quality with no significant non-operating volatility.","Strong cash generation is evident, with cash at bank increasing by 256% over the 4-year period.","The company exhibits a very conservative capital structure with a gearing ratio of only 1.14% in 2024."],"red_flags":["High customer concentration: Top 3 debtors account for over 70% of the sales ledger balance.","26.3% of the sales ledger is aged beyond 30 days, which may indicate potential working capital friction with larger clients."],"narrative":"Adam & Co presents an exceptionally strong financial profile for an acquisition target in the financial services/contracting sector. The company has achieved consistent double-digit revenue growth (22.6% CAGR) while maintaining a perfectly stable 50% gross margin, which is a rare indicator of pricing power and operational discipline. Profitability is not only growing in absolute terms but also in margin percentage, as administrative expenses have been successfully diluted against a rising revenue base. This operational gearing has resulted in an operating profit CAGR of 31.7%, significantly outperforming top-line growth.\\n\\nThe quality of earnings is high; net profit consistently follows operating trends, and the effective tax rate remains stable at 19%. The balance sheet is a particular area of strength, characterised by high liquidity (Current Ratio of 1.79) and a near-total absence of long-term debt. The interest coverage ratio of 159.1x suggests the business is currently under-leveraged, providing a significant opportunity for a buyer to utilise the company's own cash flow to service acquisition debt. 