 flags a 'capex cliff' and aging infrastructure.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":6,"case_for_inclusion":"The current EBITDA is overstated because the business is not reinvesting in its aging warehouse and chill store infrastructure.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may claim the assets are perfectly functional despite their accounting book value being zero."},{"item":"Missing Finance Function Cost","category":"missing_management","amount":15000,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"justification":"The business lacks a formal Finance Director/Controller; at £4m revenue, a part-time commercial FD or enhanced bookkeeping function is required.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":5,"case_for_inclusion":"Professionalizing the business post-acquisition requires dedicated financial oversight not currently reflected in the cost base.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue the existing accountancy fees (£6.9k) and administrative staff are sufficient for a business of this scale."}],"total_add_backs":-4424,"total_deductions":52299,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":24028,"base":24028,"optimistic":39028},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":80751,"plus_add_backs":-4424,"minus_deductions":52299,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":24028},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Owner-Director","current_salary":35201,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M: Working MD (£45k-£70k)","adjustment":22299,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":false,"key_assumptions":["Revenue decline of 9.6% can be stabilized.","Sticky overheads (Utilities, Professional Fees) can be rationalized.","The aging warehouse infrastructure does not suffer a catastrophic failure."],"sensitivity_factors":["Fuel and motor expense volatility affecting delivery margins.","Interest rate increases on the high level of HP debt for the vehicle fleet.","Supplier credit terms continuing to tighten (creditor days fell from 51 to 37)."],"upside_scenarios":["Route optimization to reduce motor expenses further.","Utilizing the modern vehicle fleet to win higher-margin specialized contracts."],"downside_scenarios":["Continued revenue erosion leads to negative EBITDA due to high fixed costs.","Immediate requirement for warehouse refurbishment (estimated £145k cost) exhausts cash."]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA of £81k is heavily inflated by under-market director pay and deferred maintenance.","The business is currently being 'milked' for dividends (£57k) that exceed net profit (£3.6k) and even adjusted EBITDA.","Operating leverage is poor; administrative expenses rose by 1.3% while revenue fell by 9.6%.","The interest coverage ratio of 2.3x provides almost no headroom for acquisition debt."],"red_flags":["96% collapse in net profit in the latest financial year.","Dividends paid are 16x the annual net profit.","Core warehouse and chill store assets are 100% depreciated and require urgent investment.","Significant revenue decline trend (-9.6% YoY)."],"narrative":"The Quality of Earnings for this Food Wholesaler is exceptionally poor. While the reported EBITDA is £81k, this figure is not 'transferable' to a buyer. Once a market-rate salary for a replacement manager is factored in and a realistic budget for maintaining aging warehouse infrastructure is applied, the 'True' EBITDA drops to approximately £24k. The business is currently in a dangerous cycle of declining revenue and rising fixed costs, while the owners are extracting cash via dividends at a rate that is eroding the company's capital base. The modern vehicle fleet is the only significant asset of value, but it is heavily encumbered by debt. A buyer would be acquiring a business with razor-thin margins and a looming requirement for significant capital expenditure."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Food Wholesaler","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":45,"confidence":"medium","ebitda_multiple_valuat