2,"equity_value":-21407},"key_customer_loss_impact":"High - given the thin 0.9% operating margin, the loss of a single major account would likely result in an operating loss.","director_replacement_impact":"Already factored into Adjusted EBITDA as a £22,299 deduction."},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":500000,"high":1000000},"seller_anchor_points":["Historical performance (2022/23 EBITDA levels)","Revenue multiple (0.2x - 0.25x turnover)","Emotional value of the established brand"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Extreme. The seller is likely anchoring on historical profits or turnover multiples, whereas the current earnings-based valuation is negligible. The deal will likely only close based on Net Asset Value (NAV) or as a distressed asset sale."},"key_findings":["Earnings-based valuation is currently unviable due to the collapse in adjusted EBITDA to £24k.","The business is effectively an asset-play, with the value residing in the vehicle fleet and working capital.","The current dividend policy is unsustainable and is actively liquidating the company's equity.","Revenue multiples are misleading here because the cost structure is too high to support the turnover."],"red_flags":["96% drop in net profit in the latest year.","Interest coverage ratio of 2.3x suggests high financial fragility.","Dividends paid (£57k) are 16x the annual net profit (£3.6k).","Core warehouse assets are 100% depreciated, implying a 'capex cliff'."],"narrative":"Valuing Food Wholesaler on an earnings basis yields a negligible result because the 'transferable' EBITDA has been eroded by falling revenue and sticky overheads. While the sector suggests multiples of 2.0x-3.5x, applying these to an adjusted EBITDA of £24k results in an Enterprise Value that doesn't even cover the company's debt and tax liabilities. Consequently, the valuation must shift to an asset-based approach. The Adjusted Net Asset Value of £243k serves as the realistic floor. However, a buyer will be wary of the 'capex cliff' regarding the warehouse and the high HP debt on the vehicles. Any deal would likely require a significant portion of the price to be deferred or contingent on stabilizing the revenue decline."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Food Wholesaler","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":38,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-backed distressed acquisition with heavy performance-based earnouts to mitigate the 96% profit collapse.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly risk-averse and views the business primarily as an asset-play (fleet and inventory) rather than a going concern.","consideration":{"total_headline":243786,"upfront_cash":73136,"upfront_percent":30,"deferred":70650,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in 2 equal installments at month 12 and 24, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":100000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Recovery","earnout_period_months":36,"earnout_rationale":"Tied to restoring Adjusted EBITDA to >£60k. Protects buyer against the current 'sticky' overheads and revenue decline.","retention_escrow":50000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months pending no undisclosed liabilities or tax issues (specifically Deferred Tax)."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in food wholesale within a 50-mile radius of the warehouse.","consultancy_arrangement":"Part-time (2 days/week) for months 3-6 at a fixed nominal fee."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from the 2024/25 dividend payments exceeding net profit.","Indemnity for any HP contract defaults or acceleration clauses triggered by change of control.","Specific indemnity for warehouse structural repairs (Capex Cliff)."],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":2500,"basket":10000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":102323,"rationale":"Given the rapid contraction in working capital and cash, a completion accounts mechanism is essential to ensure the buyer doesn't inherit a hollowed-out balance sheet."},"effective_price":{"best_case":343786,"expected_case":143786,"worst_case":73136}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"NAV-based floor price with a shared-risk earnout based on revenue stabilization.","suitable_when":"The seller accepts that the earnings-based valuation is currently unviable and agrees to a price anchored on Adjusted Net Asset Value.","consideration":{"total_headline":243786,"upfront_cash":121893,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":60946,"deferred_schedule":"Paid at month 12 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":60947,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Chosen to ensure the 9.6% revenue decline is halted. Easier to measure and harder to manipulate than EBITDA.","retention_escrow":30000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon finalization of the first-year audit post-acquisition."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Food and beverage wholesale and distribution.","consultancy_arrangement":"Ad-hoc support for key customer introductions for 6 months."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for Deferred Tax Liability (£64.7k).","Indemnity for any bad debts over 90 days not already provisioned."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":18,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":15000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":140000,"rationale":"Uses a 3-year average working capital peg to prevent the seller from further liquidating stock/cash before closing."},"effective_price":{"best_case":243786,"expected_case":182839,"worst_case":121893}},{"name":"Competitive","strategy":"Higher upfront cash to bridge the gap with seller expectations, but with strict clawbacks.","suitable_when":"There are multiple bidders and the buyer believes they can quickly fix the 0.9% margin through operational synergies.","consideration":{"total_headline":350000,"upfront_cash":245000,"upfront_percent":70,"deferred":105000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid over 12 months.","earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"None","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"Simplified structure to appeal to a seller looking for a clean exit.","retention_escrow":35000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Standard 12-month release."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":1,"non_compete_months":12,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competitors only.","consultancy_arrangement":"None."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for Deferred Tax Liability."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Provides price certainty to the seller, but requires a very recent 'locked box' balance sheet date with strict no-leakage (no dividends) covenants."},"effective_price":{"best_case":350000,"expected_case":350000,"worst_case":250000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The business is in a state of operational collapse with a 96% profit drop and a dividend policy that is actively liquidating the company. An earnings-based valuation is impossible. The Conservative structure protects the buyer by anchoring the price to the Adjusted NAV while making a significant portion of the payment contingent on the business actually returning to profitability. The completion accounts mechanism is non-negotiable to prevent further cash extraction via dividends before closing.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the condition of the Isuzu vehicle fleet and HP transferability.","Securing a significant working capital peg to ensure liquidity post-close.","Obtaining a full indemnity for the Deferred Tax Liability of £64.7k.","Immediate cessation of dividend payments (No-leakage covenant)."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal to move to a completion accounts mechanism.","Any further dividend payments prior to completion.","Discovery of significant undisclosed warehouse maintenance requirements exceeding £50k."],"key_findings":["The business is currently an asset-play with a 'broken' P&L.","Owner dependency is high, yet owners are extracting value at an unsustainable rate.","The vehicle fleet is the primary value driver, but the warehouse is a liability (Capex Cliff).","Interest coverage (2.3x) is too low to support traditional acquisition debt."],"narrative":"Food Wholesaler presents a classic 'falling knife' scenario. While the revenue is substantial at nearly £4m, the 0.9% operating margin leaves no room for error. The owners appear to be extracting capital (dividends) rather than reinvesting in the aging warehouse infrastructure. A successful deal must ignore the seller's likely high expectations based on turnover and focus strictly on the Net Asset Value. The recommended Conservative structure treats this as a turnaround/distressed play, ensuring the buyer only pays for performance that actually materializes post-acquisition."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Food Wholesaler","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":42,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2022":{"revenue":4009315,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":3148285,"gross_profit":861030,"gross_margin_percent":21.48,"administrative_expenses":688473,"operating_profit":172557,"operating_margin_percent":4.3,"depreciation_amortisation":54606,"ebitda":227163,"interest_payable":1534,"interest_coverage_ratio":112.49,"profit_before_tax":156172,"corporation_tax":32105,"effective_tax_rate_percent":20.56,"net_profit":124067,"net_margin_percent":3.09},"2023":{"revenue":4417505,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":10.18,"cost_of_sales":3415763,"gross_profit":1001742,"gross_margin_percent":22.68,"administrative_expenses":833098,"operating_profit":168644,"operating_margin_percent":3.82,"depreciation_amortisation":63416,"ebitda":232060,"interest_payable":8846,"interest_coverage_ratio":19.06,"profit_before_tax":159798,"corporation_tax":25966,"effective_tax_rate_percent":16.25,"net_profit":133832,"net_margin_percent":3.03},"2024":{"revenue":4399699,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-0.4,"cost_of_sales":3439130,"gross_profit":960569,"gross_margin_percent":21.83,"administrative_expenses":829108,"operating_profit":131461,"operating_margin_percent":2.99,"depreciation_amortisation":66652,"ebitda":198113,"interest_payable":10577,"interest_coverage_ratio":12.43,"profit_before_tax":113297,"corporation_tax":22785,"effective_tax_rate_percent":20.11,"net_profit":90512,"net_margin_percent":2.06},"2025":{"revenue":3977988,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-9.58,"cost_of_sales":3101778,"gross_profit":876210,"gross_margin_percent":22.03,"administrative_expenses":839885,"operating_profit":36325,"operating_margin_percent":0.91,"depreciation_amortisation":44426,"ebitda":80751,"interest_payable":15703,"interest_coverage_ratio":2.31,"profit_before_tax":25049,"corporation_tax":21471,"effective_tax_rate_percent":85.72,"net_profit":3578,"net_margin_percent":0.09}},"cagr":{"revenue_cagr_percent":-0.26,"gross_profit_cagr_percent":0.58,"operating_profit_cagr_percent":-40.45,"period_years":3},"cost_structure":{"cost_of_sales_percent_revenue":77.97,"overheads_percent_revenue":21.11,"staff_costs_percent_revenue":6.7,"director_costs_percent_revenue":0.88,"top_5_overheads":[{"category":"Advertising & Marketing","value":98324,"percent_of_overheads":11.71},{"category":"Professional Fees","value":91375,"percent_of_overheads":10.88},{"category":"Motor Expenses","value":90239,"percent_of_overheads":10.74},{"category":"Utilities","value":85000,"percent_of_overheads":10.12},{"category":"Rent & Rates","value":77395,"percent_of_overheads":9.21}],"cost_base_classification":"mixed"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":false,"exceptional_items_identified":["Loss on disposal of tangible fixed assets (2022, 2024)","Profit on disposal of tangible fixed assets (2025)"],"tax_rate_consistent":false,"ebitda_latest":80751,"ebitda_trend":"declining","limitations":["Amortisation not separately broken out in 2025 overheads","Effective tax rate in 2025 appears skewed by deferred tax adjustments"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":2.31,"interest_coverage_trend":"deteriorating","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Very limited. The interest coverage ratio has collapsed from 112x to 2.3x in three years. Current cash flow barely supports existing debt service."},"key_findings":["Revenue has entered a period of decline, falling 9.6% in the latest financial year.","Operating margins have collapsed from 4.3% to 0.9% due to sticky overheads against a falling revenue base.","EBITDA has declined by 65% over the last two years, significantly impacting valuation multiples.","The company is maintaining a dividend policy (£57k) that significantly exceeds net profit (£3.6k), eroding the capital base.","Cost pressures are evident in utilities and professional fees, which have risen despite falling turnover.","The vehicle fleet is relatively modern following 2023/24 investment, but this has increased interest and HP obligations.","Liquidity is tightening, with the quick ratio remaining consistently below 0.70.","Net assets decreased by 18% in the latest year, marking a reversal of previous growth trends."],"red_flags":["96% collapse in net profit between 2024 and 2025.","Interest coverage ratio at 2.3x is approaching technical default levels for typical senior debt.","Unsustainable dividend payments exceeding annual earnings.","Negative revenue trajectory combined with rising fixed costs (Utilities, Rent)."],"narrative":"The financial performance of the Food Wholesaler presents a concerning trajectory for a potential acquirer. While the company showed healthy growth and strong margins in 2022 and 2023, the last 24 months have seen a significant deterioration in earnings quality and operational efficiency. Revenue peaked in 2023 at £4.42m but has since declined to £3.98m, a nearly 10% drop in the latest year alone. More critically, the cost base has proven to be 'sticky'; administrative expenses have actually increased during the revenue downturn, resulting in a collapse of the operating margin to below 1%. EBITDA has followed this downward trend, falling from £232k to just £81k. This suggests that the business lacks the operational flexibility to scale costs down in line with volume reductions. From a debt perspective, the company is increasingly leveraged relative to its earnings. The interest coverage ratio has plummeted from over 100x to just 2.3x, leaving almost no headroom for the additional debt service typically required in an acquisition. Furthermore, the current management is extracting dividends far in excess of net earnings, which has led to an 18% reduction in net assets in the latest period. While the asset register shows a relatively modern vehicle fleet that could offer some refinancing potential, the core underlying profitability is currently insufficient to support a premium valuation. An acquirer would need to identify immediate overhead synergies or a clear path to reversing the revenue decline to justify the investment."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":58,"financialPeriodId":65,"targetCompanyId":19,"intangibleAssets":"11169","tangibleFixedAssets":"258787","freeholdProperty":"39283","leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"84481","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":"174306","computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"292748","tradeDebtors":"184568","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"2562","cashAtBank":"126648","totalCurrentAssets":"606526","tradeCreditors":"314847","taxationSocialSecurity":"33128","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"105523","hi