ofit":3668333,"net_margin_percent":14.19}},"cagr":{"revenue_cagr_percent":16.06,"gross_profit_cagr_percent":16.06,"operating_profit_cagr_percent":18.14,"period_years":4},"cost_structure":{"cost_of_sales_percent_revenue":15,"overheads_percent_revenue":54.31,"staff_costs_percent_revenue":39.99,"director_costs_percent_revenue":0.63,"top_5_overheads":[{"category":"Staff Wages & Salaries","value":10341500,"percent_of_overheads":73.64},{"category":"Advertising & Marketing","value":2541250,"percent_of_overheads":18.1},{"category":"Depreciation","value":258549,"percent_of_overheads":1.84},{"category":"Other Overheads","value":2167250,"percent_of_overheads":15.43},{"category":"Professional Fees","value":null,"percent_of_overheads":null}],"cost_base_classification":"predominantly_fixed"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":[],"tax_rate_consistent":true,"ebitda_latest":4831105,"ebitda_trend":"growing","limitations":["Detailed overhead breakdown for 2023 and 2024 is partially aggregated in source data","Depreciation not explicitly broken out in all early statutory summaries but available in management/asset data"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":104.52,"interest_coverage_trend":"improving","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Exceptional. The company has minimal existing debt and a massive interest coverage ratio, suggesting significant capacity for acquisition-related leverage."},"key_findings":["Consistent double-digit revenue growth averaging 16% CAGR over a 5-year period.","Gross margins are exceptionally stable at 85%, reflecting a high-value service model with controlled direct costs.","Operating leverage is evident as operating profit growth (18.1% CAGR) outpaces revenue growth.","Staff costs are the primary overhead, representing approximately 40% of revenue, which is typical for the sector.","Liquidity is a major strength, with a current ratio of 3.24 and £4.75m in cash as of FY2024.","The balance sheet is de-risking rapidly, with the gearing ratio falling from 28.3% in 2020 to under 4% in 2024.","Debtor management is excellent, with 100% of receivables collected within 60 days and no bad debt issues identified."],"red_flags":[],"narrative":"Brown Estate Agent presents an exceptionally strong financial profile for acquisition. The company has demonstrated consistent, organic revenue growth of 15-17% annually over the last five years, reaching £25.9m in FY2024. This growth is matched by perfectly stable gross margins of 85%, suggesting that the business possesses significant pricing power and a disciplined approach to direct costs. Operating margins have remained healthy between 16.5% and 17.8%, with clear evidence of operational leverage as the business scales.\\n\\nThe cost structure is typical for a high-touch service business, dominated by staff costs (c. 40% of revenue). While the cost base is predominantly fixed, the high margin profile provides a substantial buffer against market fluctuations. Earnings quality is high; net profit tracks operating profit closely, and the effective tax rate is consistent at 19%. EBITDA has grown from £2.49m to £4.83m over the period, providing a strong foundation for valuation.\\n\\nFrom a balance sheet perspective, the company is in a superior position. It is highly liquid, with cash reserves of £4.75m and a current ratio exceeding 3.0x. Debt levels are negligible, and the interest coverage ratio of 104.5x indicates that the business could comfortably service significant additional debt if required for the acquisition. The quality of assets is high, with a young vehicle fleet and recent investments in CRM and IT infrastructure. Overall, the financial data reveals a robust, well-managed, and highly profitable business with no visible red flags, making it a prime candidate for acquisition."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":50,"financialPeriodId":56,"targetCompanyId":15,"intangibleAssets":"52500","tangibleFixedAssets":"1402447","free