0,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M: Working MD/Owner-Director (£45k-£70k)","adjustment":32500,"adjustment_type":"add_back"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Gross margins remain stable at 29.2% despite inflationary pressures.","The 2025 distribution costs are truly non-recurring.","The buyer can successfully address the payroll-to-revenue creep."],"sensitivity_factors":["Supplier credit terms: High reliance on 94-day creditor terms; any reduction would squeeze cash.","Warehouse capacity: Aging racking limits scalability without immediate capex."],"upside_scenarios":["Automation of warehouse/logistics to reduce the 21% payroll-to-revenue ratio.","Utilising the significant debt headroom (39x interest cover) for bolt-on acquisitions."],"downside_scenarios":["Tightening of trade credit terms by major suppliers.","Failure of the aged ERP system causing operational downtime."]},"key_findings":["Exceptional gross margin consistency (29.2%) over 5 years suggests a very strong and defensible market niche.","The business is significantly over-staffed compared to its 2020 profile, with payroll costs doubling as a percentage of revenue.","Balance sheet is extremely clean with gearing below 10% and high cash reserves.","The 2025 management accounts contain a large exceptional item that significantly distorts the short-term EBITDA view."],"red_flags":["Payroll costs outstripping revenue growth consistently for 4 years.","High reliance on trade creditors (94 days) to fund the working capital cycle.","Approaching 'capex cliff' for ERP and warehouse racking systems."],"narrative":"Test Company presents as a high-quality, stable acquisition target with a very reliable gross margin profile. The primary 'Quality of Earnings' challenge is the recent creep in administrative and payroll expenses, which have eroded the operational leverage the business once enjoyed. While the reported EBITDA is £244k, the base-case adjusted EBITDA of £364k accounts for the normalisation of exceptional distribution costs and owner-related expenses. However, a buyer must be prepared for immediate capital expenditure to refresh aging IT and warehouse infrastructure. The business is a 'cash cow' with significant debt capacity, but future value will be unlocked through operational tightening rather than top-line growth alone."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Test Company","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":85,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":364360,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":2,"mid":2.75,"high":3.5},"selected_multiple":2.75,"multiple_justification":"The business sits at the mid-point of the sector range. While it demonstrates exceptional margin stability (29.2%) and a diversified customer base (HHI 1042), these premiums are offset by the small revenue scale (£3.2M), significant payroll cost creep (doubled since 2020), and approaching capex requirements for ERP and racking systems.","premium_factors_applied":["Exceptional gross margin stability (29.2% over 5 years)","Highly diversified customer base (no customer > 10%)","Strong interest coverage (39.9x) and low gearing (8.8%)","Consistent organic revenue growth (3.12% CAGR)"],"discount_factors_applied":["Small revenue scale (<£5M)","Operational inefficiency (payroll % of revenue doubled)","Aging IT and warehouse infrastructure (Capex cliff)","Key-man dependency (2-person management team)"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":573400,"base":1001990,"optimistic":1485260}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":1001990,"plus_cash":234200,"minus_long_term_debt":65000,"minus_director_loans":0,"minus_bad_debt_provision":6000,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":0,"other_adjustments":[{"item":"Deferred Maintenance Provision","amount":63500,"description":"Immediate capex required for ERP and Racking replacement"}],"equity_value":{"conservative":683100,"base":1101690,"optimi