y leak.","High reliance on 94-day creditor terms; any supplier tightening would impact the equity bridge.","Aging ERP and warehouse racking require immediate post-acquisition capital."],"narrative":"Test Company is a high-quality, low-risk acquisition target with a defensible market position evidenced by its 29.2% gross margin consistency. The valuation of £1.1M (Equity Value) reflects a healthy 2.75x multiple on adjusted earnings. While the balance sheet is exceptionally clean, the 'Quality of Earnings' adjustment is vital here; the buyer must normalize for the 2025 exceptional distribution costs to see the true earning power. The primary value-creation lever for an acquirer is operational: reversing the 4-year trend of payroll creep and modernizing the aging IT infrastructure. The business represents a stable platform for a trade buyer, though negotiations will likely hinge on the buyer's willingness to pay for the 'add-backs' versus the seller's recognition of the impending capex requirements."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Test Company","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":82,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-backed upfront with heavy performance-contingent deferred payments to mitigate payroll inefficiency and capex risks.","suitable_when":"The buyer is concerned about the 'payroll creep' and the 2025 exceptional distribution costs being recurring rather than one-off.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":675000,"upfront_percent":61.4,"deferred":125000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 12 and 24, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":300000,"earnout_metric":"Adjusted EBITDA","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Tied to achieving the 'Base Case' EBITDA of £364k. Protects buyer if the 2025 distribution costs recur or payroll costs cannot be reduced.","retention_escrow":100000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 m