"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Speeds up closing; relies on the 2023/24 balance sheet date."},"effective_price":{"best_case":150000,"expected_case":150000,"worst_case":112500}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The business is technically loss-making on an adjusted basis (-£16k EBITDA). Paying a high upfront multiple on historical 2023 earnings is dangerous given the 63% profit collapse in 2024. The Conservative structure ensures the buyer only pays for the cash and assets on hand, with any 'goodwill' premium earned only if the buyer can successfully reverse the margin compression.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the £77k cash balance at the date of offer.","Audit of the 485% utility spike to ensure no hidden arrears.","Confirmation of equipment ownership (due to zero fixed assets on BS).","Agreement on a 'Replacement Manager' salary deduction in the valuation bridge."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Significant further depletion of cash reserves before completion.","Failure to provide a valid lease for the nursery premises.","Undisclosed staff pay rises or NMW non-compliance."],"key_findings":["The business has a strong cash position but a broken business model (costs > revenue growth).","Seller expectations are likely 3-4x higher than the adjusted economic value.","The lack of fixed assets makes this a 'contract and people' acquisition with no collateral."],"narrative":"Structuring a deal for Santos Nursery requires a 'Cash-Plus' approach rather than an 'EBITDA-Multiple' approach. Because the adjusted EBITDA is negative, the primary value sits in the £77k cash and the nursery license. A Conservative structure is essential to prevent the buyer from overpaying for a business that is currently consuming its own capital. The earnout must be the primary vehicle for meeting the seller's high price expectations, shifting the risk of the 2024 margin recovery onto the seller."},"financial":{"expert":"financ