_of_overheads":2.54},{"category":"Utilities","value":8715,"percent_of_overheads":2.54},{"category":"Other Overheads","value":7203,"percent_of_overheads":2.1}],"cost_base_classification":"predominantly_fixed"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":["Other operating income of 17,525 in 2022"],"tax_rate_consistent":false,"ebitda_latest":36118,"ebitda_trend":"declining","limitations":["Depreciation and Amortisation not separately disclosed","Corporation tax not disclosed in P&L","Director remuneration not explicitly separated from staff costs"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":null,"interest_coverage_trend":"stable","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Limited. While the company has reduced bank loans, the sharp decline in 2024 operating profit reduces the buffer for servicing new acquisition debt."},"key_findings":["Revenue growth has decelerated sharply from 36.2% in 2023 to 3.5% in 2024.","Operating margins experienced extreme volatility, peaking at 23.8% in 2023 before crashing to 8.5% in 2024.","Staff costs are the primary driver of margin compression, increasing by 28.4% in 2024 despite minimal revenue growth.","Utility costs spiked by 485% in the latest year, indicating significant exposure to energy price inflation.","The business successfully transitioned from a net liability position in 2022 to positive net assets by 2023.","Liquidity has improved significantly with a current ratio of 2.18 in 2023, up from 0.32.","Cost of Sales increased by 78.6% in 2024, suggesting a loss of control over direct procurement or pricing."],"red_flags":["Severe margin compression in 2024 (Net Margin fell from 23.8% to 8.5%).","Staff costs growing at 8x the rate of revenue growth in the latest period.","Significant spike in utility and cost of sales without corresponding revenue uplift.","Lack of transparency regarding depreciation and tax provisions in the provided accounts."],"narrative":"Santos Nursery presents a financial profile characterized by a strong recovery in 2023 followed by concerning operational slippage in 2024. The company achieved an impressive 36.2% revenue jump in 2023, which, combined with disciplined cost management, allowed it to exit a net liability position and build a healthy cash reserve of £77,797. However, the 2024 results suggest that the business is struggling to pass on inflationary pressures to its customers. While revenue remained stable (3.5% growth), the cost base expanded aggressively. Staff wages, which represent nearly 80% of overheads, rose by £60k, and utility costs saw a near five-fold increase. This has resulted in a 63% collapse in net profit year-on-year. From an M&A perspective, the high gross margins (89%+) are attractive, but the high fixed-cost nature of the business makes it highly sensitive to occupancy levels and wage inflation. A buyer must investigate whether the 2024 margin compression is a temporary 'catch-up' on costs or a permanent shift in the business's profitability profile. The lack of debt service data (interest) and depreciation makes a formal EBITDA valuation difficult without further disclosure, though the underlying cash generation appears to have weakened significantly in the last 12 months."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":77,"financialPeriodId":91,"targetCompanyId":24,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":null,"prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"21671","cashAtBank":"77797","totalCurrentAssets":"99468","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":"566","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"26671","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":"18300","amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":null,"t