25,"justification":"The TUEPEN Spider MEWP is at 24% NBV and represents a 'capex cliff'. An annual provision for specialized equipment replacement is necessary.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":7,"case_for_inclusion":"The current depreciation charge is low because assets are aging; a realistic maintenance/replacement fund is needed for sustainability.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue that the 2025 fleet refresh already addressed the most urgent equipment needs."}],"total_add_backs":107569,"total_deductions":120000,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":57700,"base":69124,"optimistic":102500},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":81555,"plus_add_backs":107569,"minus_deductions":120000,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":69124},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"David Greener","current_salary":6288,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Working MD/Owner-Director (£1M-£5M range mid-point)","adjustment":51212,"adjustment_type":"deduction"},{"name":"Helen","current_salary":6288,"estimated_market_rate":47500,"benchmark_range_used":"General Manager/Admin (£1M-£5M range mid-point)","adjustment":41212,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Gross margin remains above 53% by maintaining in-house labour model","Revenue growth continues at historical CAGR of 6.4%","Debtor days normalize back to <15 days from the 2025 spike of 35 days"],"sensitivity_factors":["Recruitment of skilled grounds operatives to replace subcontractor flexibility","Retention of key contracts managed personally by David Greener"],"upside_scenarios":["Professionalizing the sales function could accelerate growth beyond 6%","Optimizing creditor days (currently 2.6) to industry standard (30) would significantly boost cash flow"],"downside_scenarios":["Failure to replace the MEWP leads to loss of high-margin 'Reach & Wash' or specialized maintenance work","Loss of the Grounds Maintenance Manager who holds the operational knowledge"]},"key_findings":["Underlying EBITDA is masked by high discretionary pension contributions (£64k) and one-off asset losses (£32k).","The strategic shift to in-house labour has successfully expanded gross margins from 44.9% to 55.4%.","The business is debt-free with a strong current ratio (2.97), providing a clean platform for acquisition.","Owner dependency is the primary operational risk, with both directors performing critical, non-redundant roles."],"red_flags":["Debtor days spiked from 5 to 35 in 2025, suggesting potential collection issues or customer distress.","Dividends exceeded net profit in 2025, leading to a 22.4% erosion of net assets.","Management accounts for 2026 are incomplete (100% margins), indicating a breakdown in bookkeeping discipline."],"narrative":"Greener Estates is a high-quality service business with a strong margin profile. While reported 2025 EBITDA is £81,555, this figure is heavily distorted by owner-managed accounting. We have identified £107,569 in defensible add-backs, primarily relating to discretionary pensions and a one-off loss on asset disposal. However, these are offset by £120,000 in necessary deductions to reflect the cost of a professional management team to replace the founders. The resulting Base Case Adjusted EBITDA of £69,124 represents the sustainable earnings power of the business under new ownership. The primary risk for a buyer is the 'management gap'—the business currently lacks the middle management required to operate without the founders. Provided a transition plan is in place for David Greener's sales contacts and Helen's administrative processes, the earnings are considered highly sustainable."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Greener Estates","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":72,"confidence":"medium","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":69124,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2.25,"multiple_just