kely £450k+ expectation, using a 'stretch' earnout.","suitable_when":"The buyer is confident in their ability to professionalize the business and wants to win against other bidders.","consideration":{"total_headline":320000,"upfront_cash":192000,"upfront_percent":60,"deferred":32000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid 6 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":96000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Growth > £80k","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Allows the seller to achieve a higher price if they help the buyer scale the business beyond current levels.","retention_escrow":10000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon finalization of the first set of post-completion management accounts."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":12,"non_compete_scope":"Restricted to existing client list only.","consultancy_arrangement":"Ad-hoc consultancy for 6 months on a per-diem basis."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for any 2026 management account inaccuracies (100% margin issue)."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":10000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":88000,"rationale":"Simplifies the closing process to appeal to a seller looking for a clean exit."},"effective_price":{"best_case":320000,"expected_case":224000,"worst_case":182000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The combination of extreme owner dependency (both directors), a 7x spike in debtor days, and the lack of middle management makes an upfront-heavy deal too risky. The Conservative structure uses an escrow to specifically target the debtor risk and an earnout to ensure the founders stay long enough to institutionalize their knowledge.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the £43k debtor balance and its collectability.","Securing a long-term handover from Helen to document back-office SOPs.","Agreement on the 'Management Replacement' deductions in the EBITDA calculation.","Physical inspection and valuation of the TUEPEN Spider MEWP."],"deal_breaker_terms":["If the £43k debtor balance is found to be a single disputed or uncollectable invoice.","If the 2026 management accounts reveal a significant margin collapse once costs are properly accrued.","Refusal of the sellers to provide a minimum 12-month transition period."],"key_findings":["The business is debt-free but capital-eroded due to aggressive dividend payouts.","High gross margins (55%) are the primary value driver but are vulnerable to labor turnover.","The 'Management Gap' requires a £120k investment in new staff, which must be reflected in the price.","The balance sheet cash (£104k) is a significant buffer but is currently being used to fund owner lifestyle rather than growth."],"narrative":"Greener Estates is a classic 'lifestyle' business that has reached its ceiling under current ownership. While the financial health is superficially strong (debt-free, high margins), the operational risks are concentrated in the two founders. A successful deal must bridge the gap between the sellers' emotional valuation (likely based on revenue) and the buyer's investment reality (based on maintainable EBITDA after management replacement). The Conservative structure is recommended to ensure the buyer does not overpay for a business that might lose its primary contracts or operational capability the moment the founders exit."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Greener Estates","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":72,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2021":{"revenue":347643,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":177997,"gross_profit":169646,"gross_margin_percent":48.8,"administrative_expenses":86925,"operating_profit":81229,"operating_margin_percent":23.37,"depreciation_amortisation":13377,"ebitda":94606,"interest_payable":0,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":81247,"corporation_tax":13648,"effective_tax_rate_pe