ngs.","High gearing relative to the thin earnings base and declining net assets."],"narrative":"Goldwire Financial Solutions Limited presents a profile of high-volume, low-margin growth that has failed to achieve operational scale. While the 45% revenue CAGR is superficially impressive, the underlying financial health is concerning. The most critical issue is the systematic compression of the gross margin, which has fallen from 33.4% to 13.8%. This suggests that as the company scales, it is losing control over its direct costs—primarily subcontractors—or is forced to price aggressively to win business in a commoditised market.\\n\\nProfitability is marginal at best. With a net margin of just 1.04%, the business has no safety buffer. Furthermore, the quality of the balance sheet has deteriorated significantly in the latest period. The decision to move £185,000 into intercompany loans has stripped the business of its liquidity, leaving it with a quick ratio of 0.09. This, combined with a dividend policy that regularly exceeds annual net profit, indicates a strategy of capital extraction rather than reinvestment. For an acquirer, the business offers a significant customer base but requires a complete overhaul of the cost structure and a stabilisation of margins. The current earnings are too thin to support any meaningful acquisition debt, and the reliance on intercompany receivables for working capital poses a significant integration risk."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":79,"financialPeriodId":94,"targetCompanyId":18,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"14827","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":"0","motorVehicles":"14827","computerEquipment":"0","stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"1400","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":"185000","directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"750","cashAtBank":"13239","totalCurrentAssets":"200389","tradeCreditors":"62241","taxati