00,"deferred_schedule":"Paid at month 12.","earnout_maximum":150000,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Targets","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Simple revenue-based earnout to align with seller's growth narrative.","retention_escrow":50000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released at month 12."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":12,"non_compete_scope":"General property maintenance.","consultancy_arrangement":"Minimal transition support."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Standard fundamental warranties only."],"warranty_cap_percent":25,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":20000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":22962,"rationale":"Provides price certainty to the seller, using the most recent balance sheet date."},"effective_price":{"best_case":400000,"expected_case":325000,"worst_case":150000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The business is currently 'overtrading' with a quick ratio below 1.0 and a hollow balance sheet. The £124k in director loans effectively wipes out the equity value. A conservative structure is the only way to protect the buyer from a liquidity crisis immediately post-acquisition while forcing the sellers to remain skin-in-the-game to prove the validity of the £242k debtor book.","negotiation_priorities":["Subordination or conversion of the £124,556 Director Loans.","Verification of the 'Intangible Assets' (£75k) which currently support the entire net worth.","Establishing a strict Working Capital Peg to ensure the business is not handed over with zero cash.","Securing a long-term non-compete to protect the Heating & Plumbing customer base."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal to subordinate director loans.","Any further deterioration of the quick ratio below 0.95 prior to completion.","Discovery of significant aged debt (>90 days) within the £242k trade debtor balance."],"key_findings":["The business is technically solvent only due to £75k of intangible assets.","Liquidity is critical; the business relies entirely on daily debtor collections to pay creditors.","The 'Equity Value' is negligible once director loans are accounted for.","High owner dependency makes a long handover or earn-out essential for knowledge transfer."],"narrative":"Hub Property Care is a high-growth but fragile entity. While the £2.26M revenue is impressive, the business is 'running hot' with no capital reserves and fully depreciated assets. The deal must be structured as a 'debt-and-earn-out' play rather than a traditional cash-at-completion acquisition. The primary goal for the buyer is to secure the revenue platform while ensuring the sellers' historical debts (Director Loans) do not trigger a cash-flow collapse post-sale."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Hub Property Care","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":68,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2022":{"revenue":1473225,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":1180587,"gross_profit":292638,"gross_margin_percent":19.86,"administrative_expenses":312295,"operating_profit":-19657,"operating_margin_percent":-1.33,"depreciation_amortisation":5006,"ebitda":-14651,"interest_payable":585,"interest_coverage_ratio":-33.6,"profit_before_tax":-28195,"corporation_tax":null,"effective_tax_rate_percent":null,"net_profit":-28195,"net_margin_percent":-1.91},"2023":{"revenue":1922312,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":30.48,"cost_of_sales":1566593,"gross_profit":355719,"gross_margin_percent":18.5,"administrative_expenses":333449,"operating_profit":22270,"operating_margin_percent":1.16,"depreciation_amortisation":3103,"ebitda":25373,"interest_payable":1704,"interest_coverage_ratio":13.07,"profit_before_tax":20224,"corporation_tax":null,"effective_tax_rate_percent":null,"net_profit":20224,"net_margin_percent":1.05},"2024":{"revenue":2093149,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":8.89,"cost_of_sales":1669293,"gross_profit":423856,"gross_margin_perc