pacity_assessment":"Strong interest coverage suggests capacity for additional debt, though tightening liquidity on the balance sheet may limit lender appetite."},"key_findings":["Revenue has grown consistently from £1.47m to £2.26m, representing a healthy 15.35% CAGR.","The business successfully pivoted from an operating loss in 2022 to stable profitability in 2024-2025.","Gross margins are remarkably consistent, hovering around the 19-20% mark, suggesting stable pricing power.","Direct labour is the primary cost driver, increasing significantly in 2025 to £801k (35% of revenue).","Overhead absorption has improved, with administrative expenses falling as a percentage of revenue since 2022.","Director remuneration is high relative to net profit, representing a significant potential 'add-back' for valuation purposes.","The business model is highly variable, with 80% of revenue consumed by direct delivery costs (materials and labour)."],"red_flags":["Liquidity is tightening significantly; the quick ratio fell to 0.99 in 2025, indicating immediate liabilities exceed liquid assets.","Net current assets have eroded from £127k in 2022 to just £23k in 2025.","High reliance on trade debtors (69% of current assets) creates significant cash flow risk if collections slow.","Tangible asset base is negligible, with the balance sheet supported primarily by intangible goodwill."],"narrative":"Hub Property Care presents a profile of a maturing service business that has successfully navigated a turnaround from its 2022 loss-making position. The revenue trajectory is positive, with a 15.35% CAGR and a core Heating & Plumbing division providing a solid foundation. Profitability has stabilised at a modest 2.3-2.6% net margin; however, this is heavily influenced by a high director salary draw. From an M&A perspective, the 'Adjusted EBITDA' is likely much higher than the statutory figures suggest, as the current director remuneration (£183k) likely exceeds market rates for a replacement manager.\\n\\nWhile the P&L shows stability, the Balance Sheet requires caution. There is a clear trend of tightening liquidity, with the current ratio dropping from 1.79 to 1.07 over four years. The quick ratio of 0.99 suggests the company is operating with very little cash headroom, relying almost entirely on the timely collection of trade debtors to meet its obligations. The reclassification of directors' loans in 2024 improved the gearing ratio, but the underlying cash position remains thin. An acquirer should focus on working capital management post-acquisition to ensure the growth in revenue does not further strain the cash cycle. Overall, the financial performance is stable and predictable, but the lack of tangible assets and tightening liquidity makes this a 'moderate risk' acquisition focused on cash-flow yield rather than asset backing."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":95,"financialPeriodId":120,"targetCompanyId":28,"intangibleAssets":"75350","tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":"6109","stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"242983","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"25504","cashAtBank":"80961","totalCurrentAssets":"349448","tradeCreditors":"92534","taxationSocialSecurity":"109396","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"124556","totalCurrentLiabilities":"326486","bankLoansLongTerm":"30556","hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":"0","totalLongTermLiabilities":"30556","shareCapital":"3","retainedEarnings":"56163","totalEquity":"73865","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":134,"createdAt":"2026-03-24T20:20:12.724Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-24T20:20: