ery.","Significant 'Correction' entries in management accounts suggest potential weaknesses in the financial close process."],"narrative":"Surrey Ceiling demonstrates strong underlying trading performance, but the 'headline' EBITDA of £247k requires a downward adjustment to £197k (Base Case) to reflect a sustainable owner-managed run rate. The most significant adjustment is the £48k required to bring the director's salary to market rates, as the current remuneration is purely tax-driven. While the business is highly efficient and cash-positive, the aging fleet and high debtor concentration with Knowledge Properties Ltd present near-term risks. However, the 20% revenue CAGR and robust 57% gross margins suggest a healthy core business. A buyer should focus on the 'Corrections' entry in the 2026 accounts during due diligence to ensure 2025 earnings aren't benefiting from similar accounting anomalies."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Surrey Ceiling","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":78,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":197314,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2.25,"multiple_justification":"A mid-range sector multiple is applied. While the 20% CAGR and high margins suggest a premium, these are offset by significant micro-cap risks including high customer concentration (42% with one client) and owner dependency.","premium_factors_applied":["Strong 20% Revenue CAGR over 4 years","High operating margins (29.3% in 2025) compared to sector average","Negative cash conversion cycle indicating high capital efficiency","Successful diversification into higher-margin wholesale (20% of revenue)"],"discount_factors_applied":["High customer concentration (Knowledge Properties Ltd at 42.7% of debtors)","Micro-cap scale (Revenue <£1M) limiting institutional buyer interest","Significant key-man risk with 30-year owner relationships","Aging vehicle fleet (76% of asset cost) requiring near-term CAPEX"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":271995,"base":443956,"optimistic":638937}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":443956,"plus_cash":259000,"minus_long_term_debt":0,"minus_director_loans":1552,"minus_bad_debt_provision":6737,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":180036,"other_adjustments":[{"item":"Intercompany Balance Exclusion","amount":180036,"reason":"The £180k owed by CMJ Global is treated as a debt-like item/non-operating asset adjustment as its recoverability is uncertain and it is not required for core operations."}],"equity_value":{"conservative":342670,"base":514631,"optimistic":709612}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":317681,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":-6737,"adjusted_nav":310944,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":795066,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.3,"high":0.7},"implied_ev_range":{"low":238520,"high":556546}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":350000,"equity_value_mid":515000,"equity_value_high":710000},"primary_methodology":"ebitda_multiple","cross_check_alignment":"strong"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":488352,"equity_value":559027},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":399560,"equity_value":470235},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":542613,"equity_value":613288},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":345299,"equity_value":415974},"key_customer_loss_impact":-189569,"director_replacement_impact":-108591},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":800000,"high":1200000},"seller_anchor_points":["2025 Reported EBITDA of £247k (ignoring salary adjustments)","Strong 34% recent revenue growth","Emotional value of 30-year client relationships","Cash balance of £259k plus intercompany loan of £180k"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. The seller likely views the business as worth £1M+ based on 'headline' EBITDA and cash. A buyer will focus on the £48k salary adjustment and the £180k intercompany risk, creating a ~£300k-£500k valuation gap."},"key_findings":["The business is highly efficient with a negative cash conversion cycle, meaning growth is self-funding.","Adjusted EBITDA (Base: £197k) is significantly lower than reported (£247k) due to the necessity of a market-rate MD salary.","The £180k intercompany loan is a major deal point; if unrecoverable, it significantly reduces the equity value.","Revenue growth is accelerating (34.6% in 2025), providing a strong narrative for future performance."],"red_flags":["42.7% debtor concentration with Knowledge Properties Ltd creates a 'single point of failure' risk.","Aggressive dividend policy has historically exceeded net profits, though 2025 showed stabilization.","Aging vehicle fleet suggests a 'Capex Cliff' within the next 24-36 months.","Significant 'Correction' entries in 2026 management accounts suggest potential accounting volatility."],"narrative":"Surrey Ceiling is a high-performing specialist subcontractor that presents a classic 'small business' valuation challenge. On a headline basis, the company looks exceptional with 20% CAGR and 29% operating margins. However, once the owner's salary is normalized to market rates and the high customer concentration is factored into the multiple, the Enterprise Value settles at approximately £444k (2.25x EBITDA). The equity value is bolstered by a strong cash position but complicated by a large £180k intercompany loan that most buyers will exclude from the 'Cash-Free Debt-Free' calculation. A fair deal likely sits around the £515k mark, though bridging the gap from the seller's likely £1M+ expectation will require a structured earn-out tied to the retention of the primary client, Knowledge Properties Ltd."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Surrey Ceiling","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":58,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Maximum buyer protection with heavy emphasis on custome