ompete_months":12,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competitors within the Leicester area.","consultancy_arrangement":"None required."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Standard fundamental warranties only (Title, Capacity, Tax)."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":50000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":900000,"rationale":"Simplifies the closing process and appeals to a seller's desire for speed and certainty."},"effective_price":{"best_case":2200000,"expected_case":2200000,"worst_case":2100000}}],"recommended_structure":"Balanced","recommendation_rationale":"The Balanced structure addresses the 'Valuation Paradox' identified in the inputs. It pays the seller for the tangible value (Net Assets) while protecting the buyer against the 'lifestyle' risks (owner dependency and revenue decline) through a 12-month EBITDA-based earnout. This aligns the sellers' exit with the successful transition of the business to a professional management layer.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the £835k debtor balance and aging.","Agreement on the 'Normalised Working Capital' peg to ensure the £774k cash isn't depleted before completion.","Securing a commitment for a 6-12 month handover to mitigate the 47.8% director-payroll dependency.","Clarification on the £286k deferred tax liability and its impact on future cash flows."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal of a bad debt indemnity for debtors over 90 days.","Any further dividend extraction prior to completion (Leakage).","Failure to provide a detailed sales ledger for customer concentration analysis."],"key_findings":["The business is an asset-rich 'lifestyle' company with significant profit extraction via pensions.","Revenue decline of 9.8% is the primary valuation risk.","High liquidity and zero debt make the company highly 'bankable' for acquisition finance.","Owner dependency is extreme, requiring a structured handover and management replacement provision."],"narrative":"Printing Company (C) is a classic SME acquisition target where the balance sheet strength (Property + Cash) exceeds the earnings-based valuation. A successful deal must bridge the gap between the seller's likely £2.5m+ expectation and the £1.9m earnings-based reality. By using a 'Balanced' structure, the buyer can offer a headline price that nears the seller's expectations while ensuring that the premium paid over the Net Asset Value is only realized if the business remains stable post-acquisition. The primary focus of the SPA should be on protecting the working capital (specifically the cash and debtors) and ensuring the departing directors do not leave a management vacuum."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Printing Company (C)","analysis_date":"2025-07-20","score":68,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2021":{"revenue":3415381,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":2079700,"gross_profit":1335681,"gross_margin_percent":39.11,"administrative_expenses":1305053,"operating_profit":193300,"operating_margin_percent":5.66,"depreciation_amortisation":null,"ebitda":null,"interest_payable":1910,"interest_coverage_ratio":101.2,"profit_before_tax":191403,"corporation_tax":13437,"effective_tax_rate_percent":7.02,"net_profit":177966,"net_margin_percent":5.21},"2022":{"revenue":3361752,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-1.57,"cost_of_sales":2262171,"gross_profit":1099581,"gross_margin_percent":32.71,"administrative_expenses":1149694,"operating_profit":-23234,"operating_margin_percent":-0.69,"depreciation_amortisation":265766,"ebitda":242532,"interest_payable":1014,"interest_coverage_ratio":-22.91,"profit_before_tax":-24240,"corporation_tax":288911,"effective_tax_rate_percent":-1191.88,"net_profit":-313151,"net_margin_percent":-9.32},"2023":{"revenue":3273415,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-2.63,"cost_of_sales":2157689,"gross_profit":1115726,"gross_margin_percent":34.08,"administrative_expenses":1027907,"operating_