lowing an exceptional 2024 surge.","Gross margins are volatile, ranging from 14.5% to 23.0%, suggesting sensitivity to material costs and subcontractor pricing.","The business demonstrates high operational resilience, maintaining a debt-free balance sheet throughout the period.","Overhead growth in 2025 (up 37.5%) was driven by a 62% increase in staff-related costs, indicating investment in capacity.","Liquidity significantly improved in 2025, with the current ratio rising to 2.59 and cash reserves increasing to £390k.","Dividend policy is aggressive, with 2025 payouts representing nearly 79% of net profit, limiting internal capital compounding.","Management accounts for 2026 suggest a significant margin expansion (47.7% gross), though this requires verification against full-year statutory adjustments."],"red_flags":["Significant customer concentration: One debtor represents over 40% of the total sales ledger balance.","Sharp margin compression in 2024 (down to 14.5%) highlights vulnerability to direct cost inflation or project mispricing.","Motor expenses and insurance costs have shown extreme volatility, with motor costs increasing 370% in a single year."],"narrative":"Goodwin Tanks Limited presents a profile of a scaling engineering services firm with strong top-line momentum but fluctuating profitability. The 24.2% revenue CAGR is impressive, particularly the 83.6% surge in 2024, which appears to have been supported by a heavy reliance on subcontractors. While revenue corrected by 10% in 2025, the business successfully defended its net margin at 4.4% by improving gross efficiency, even as it significantly increased its fixed cost base through staff recruitment and training. The earnings quality is high, with operating profit translating cleanly to net income, and the absence of external debt provides a 'clean' entry for a buyer. However, the aggressive dividend policy suggests the current shareholders are extracting most of the free cash flow rather than reinvesting for growth. From an M&A perspective, the primary risks are the high customer concentration and the volatility of the gross margin. A buyer should focus on the sustainability of the 2026 management account margins, which appear significantly higher than historical norms. Overall, the company is a stable, profitable, and liquid acquisition target with substantial debt capacity."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":262,"financialPeriodId":312,"targetCompanyId":61,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"77261","tradeDebtors":"491933","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":"100715.23","directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"31064.01","cashAtBank":"572311.87","totalCurrentAssets":"1273285.11","tradeCreditors":"61127.42","taxationSocialSecurity":"60350.45","vatPayable":"-15264.72","corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"61403.18","totalCurrentLiabilities":"167616.33","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":"9665.56","otherLongTermDebt":"95884","totalLongTermLiabilities":"105549.56","shareCapital":"3100","retainedEarnings":"1159244.42","totalEquity":"1162344.42","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":352,"createdAt":"2026-04-06T22:00:27.639Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-06T22:00:27.639Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-04-06 22:07:16.542929	2026-04-15 14:12:54.374	share_sale
