, a working MD/Owner-Director market rate mid-point is £57,500.","confidence":"high","defensibility_score":8,"case_for_inclusion":"A buyer will need to employ a professional manager or compensate themselves at market rates to replace the current owners.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue that the business can be run by existing staff without a high-salaried MD."},{"item":"Deferred Maintenance / Capex Catch-up","category":"deferred_maintenance","amount":15000,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"justification":"Plant and machinery is fully depreciated (NBV £1) and the depreciation charge exceeds recent additions, indicating an aging asset base requiring higher maintenance or replacement.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":6,"case_for_inclusion":"The business is running on 'tired' assets that will require increased cash outlays to maintain current operational capacity.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller will argue that the assets are functional and the current maintenance spend is sufficient."}],"total_add_backs":153000,"total_deductions":72500,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":338501,"base":371501,"optimistic":386501},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":291001,"plus_add_backs":153000,"minus_deductions":72500,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":371501},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Combined Directors","current_salary":33000,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M: Working MD (£45k-£70k)","adjustment":24500,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Revenue stabilizes at £1.3M+ following the 2024 dip.","Gross margins remain resilient at ~48% despite inflationary pressures.","The shift to domestic installations (46.5% of revenue) does not further erode margins through higher labor intensity."],"sensitivity_factors":["High dependency on motor vehicle fleet (91% of asset NBV).","Working capital cycle lengthening (13.5 to 23.5 days).","Owner-dependency remains high with no clear middle management tier."],"upside_scenarios":["Utilizing £307k cash reserves to modernize plant and machinery to increase efficiency.","Professionalizing the sales function to reduce revenue volatility."],"downside_scenarios":["Immediate capex requirement for vehicle fleet replacement.","Loss of technical expertise if owners exit without a long handover."]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA is significantly understated in 2025 due to a one-off £120k pension contribution.","The business is effectively debt-free, providing significant headroom for acquisition financing.","Revenue volatility (21% drop in 2024) is the primary commercial risk to earnings sustainability.","The owners have been aggressively extracting capital (£231k dividends in 2024), suggesting a 'harvest' phase."],"red_flags":["Plant and Machinery is fully depreciated to £1, indicating a 'capex cliff'.","Staff costs rose in 2024 despite a 21% revenue drop, suggesting a rigid fixed-cost base.","Working capital intensity is increasing, with WC as % of revenue rising from 10.6% to 16.6%."],"narrative":"Cordell Engineering's quality of earnings is generally high but requires significant normalization of owner-related costs. The 2025 reported EBITDA of £291k is masked by a discretionary £120k pension contribution. Once adjusted for market-rate management salaries and the removal of owner-specific benefits, the Base Case Adjusted EBITDA sits at £371.5k. While the balance sheet is exceptionally clean and liquid, the 'tired' nature of the physical assets (specifically plant and machinery) and the recent revenue volatility suggest that a portion of the earnings is being generated by under-investing in the future of the business. A buyer should focus on the sustainability of the 49% gross margin and the immediate capex requirements post-completion."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Cordell Engineering","analysis_date":"2025-05-23","score":75,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":371501,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2.25,"multiple_justification":"The selected multiple of 2.25x (sector mid-point) reflects a balance between the company's excellent profitability and debt-free status against significant risks including revenue volatility, aging assets, and high owner dependency. While margins are superior to the sector average, the sub-£2M revenue scale and 'lifestyle' management characteristics prevent a premium multiple.","premium_factors_applied":["High and stable gross margins (~49%)","Debt-free balance sheet with high liquidity","Strong interest coverage history","Niche technical expertise in electrical/electronic engineering"],"discount_factors_applied":["Revenue volatility (21% drop in 2024)","Micro-SME scale (<£2M revenue, <20 staff)","High owner dependency and lack of middle management","Aging asset base (Plant & Machinery NBV at £1)","Aggressive historical dividend extraction"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":557252,"base":835877,"optimistic":1114503}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":835877,"plus_cash":307000,"minus_long_term_debt":0,"minus_director_loans":5787,"minus_bad_debt_provision":0,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":31090,"equity_value":{"conservative":827375,"base":1106000,"optimistic":1384626}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":635000,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":0,"adjusted_nav":635000,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":1310453,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.3,"high":0.7},"implied_ev_range":{"low":393136,"high":917317}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":850000,"equity_value_mid":1100000,"equity_value_high":1350000},"primary_methodology":"ebitda_multiple","cross_check_alignment":"strong"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":919465,"equity_value":1189588},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":752289,"equity_value":1022412},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":1021628,"equity_value":1291751},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":650127,"equity_value":920250},"key_customer_loss_impact":"High. Given the 21% revenue drop in 2024, the loss of a single major installation contract could reduce EBITDA by an estimated £100k-£150k, potentially wiping out 30-40% of the valuation.","director_replacement_impact":"The EBITDA has already been adjusted for a £57.5k market-rate MD salary. However, if two directors are replaced, an additional £45k-£60k deduction would be required, reducing EV by approx. £100k-£135k."},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":1500000,"high":2500000},"seller_anchor_points":["Historical peak revenue of £1.6M in 2023","High cash balance of £307k","Emotional value of a long-standing engineering firm","Reported EBITDA margins of 22% in 2025"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. Sellers are likely to anchor on a 5x-6x multiple of reported (unadjusted) EBITDA or a multiple of turnover. The gap between the fair equity value (~£1.1M) and expected price (~£1.8M+) will likely require an earn-out structure to bridge, specifically tied to the recovery of revenue to 2023 levels."},"key_findings":["The business is highly profitable with a normalized EBITDA margin of ~28%, significantly above sector averages.","Valuation is heavily supported by a strong cash position (£307k) and zero debt, which adds nearly 30% to the Enterprise Value.","The 'Capex Cliff' regarding plant and machinery (NBV £1) is a hidden liability that a buyer will use to negotiate the price downward.","Revenue volatility is the primary risk; the 2024 dip suggests the business lacks a stable, recurring revenue base."],"red_flags":["Aggressive dividend extraction in 2024 (£231k) suggests owners are de-risking ahead of a sale.","Plant and machinery are fully depreciated, indicating immediate post-acquisition investment is required.","Working capital cycle is lengthening, with stock and debtor days increasing as a percentage of revenue."],"narrative":"Cordell Engineering is a high-margin, debt-free micro-SME that presents a classic 'lifestyle' business profile. While the underlying profitability is excellent (Adjusted EBITDA of £371.5k), the valuation is constrained by the company's small scale and the inherent risks of owner-dependency and revenue volatility. The base Enterprise Value of £836k reflects a 2.25x multiple, which is fair for a technical service firm of this size. The final Equity Value of £1.1M is bolstered significantly by the company's 'clean' balance sheet and high cash reserves. However, a buyer must be wary of the aging asset base and the recent aggressive capital extraction by the current owners. A deal structure involving a significant upfront payment for the net assets plus an earn-out based on maintaining the 2025 revenue levels would be the most prudent approach."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Cordell Engineering","analysis_date":"2025-05-24","score":65,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-heavy protection with high earnout weighting to mitigate revenue volatility and owner dependency.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 21% revenue drop in 2024 and the 'capex cliff' regarding plant and machinery.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":550000,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":200000,"deferred_schedule":"Two equal installments of £100k at 12 and 24 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":350000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Floor & Revenue Stability","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Revenue Volatility (21% drop in 2024) and Owner Dependency. Earnout ensures the business maintains a normalized EBITDA of £371k without the current directors' personal involvement.","retention_escrow":110000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months pending no warranty claims related to tax or undisclosed liabilities."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Engineering and technical services within a 50-mile radius; no solicitation of existing clients or staff.","consultancy_arrangement":"Directors retained on a part-time consultancy basis for months 7-12 at a fixed day rate."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for immediate replacement of fully depreciated Plant & Machinery","Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from aggressive dividend extraction in 2024","Indemnity for potential bad debt on trade debtors over 90 days"],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":217698,"rationale":"Due to the lengthening cash conversion cycle and recent inventory spikes, completion accounts are necessary to ensure the buyer does not inherit a working capital deficit."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1100000,"expected_case":925000,"worst_case":550000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"Standard SME structure with a mix of upfront cash and performance-linked deferred payments.","suitable_when":"Due diligence confirms the 2025 recovery is sustainable and the customer base is diversified.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":770000,"upfront_percent":70,"deferred":165000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in full at 12 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":165000,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Revenue Volatility. Specifically tied to maintaining revenue at or above £1.3M to prove the 2024 dip was an anomaly.","retention_escrow":55000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon finalization of first-year statutory accounts."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in technical engineering services.","consultancy_arrangement":"Ad-hoc consultancy for technical troubleshooting for 12 months."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for 2024 dividend tax compliance","Indemnity for specific aging plant assets"],"warranty_cap_percent":30,"warranty_period_months":18,"de_minimis":7500,"basket":15000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":185000,"rationale":"Reflects a 3-year average of working capital requirements to normalize for the 2024 inventory spike."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1100000,"expected_case":1017500,"worst_case":770000}},{"name":"Competitive","strategy":"High upfront cash offer to bridge the gap with seller expectations, utilizing the company's own cash reserves.","suitable_when":"The buyer has high confidence in the technical niche and wants to pre-empt other bidders.","consideration":{"total_headline":1250000,"upfront_cash":1000000,"upfront_percent":80,"deferred":250000,"deferred_schedule":"Unconditional fixed payment at 12 months.","earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"None","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"No earnout included to make the offer more attractive to sellers who are currently in a 'harvest' phase.","retention_escrow":50000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Standard 12-month release."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition only.","consultancy_arrangement":"None required beyond handover."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["General tax indemnity"],"warranty_cap_percent":20,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":20000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Locked box at the latest management accounts date to provide price certainty to the seller, provided no 'leakage' (dividends) occurs between box date and completion."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1250000,"expected_case":1250000,"worst_case":1000000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The Conservative structure is recommended due to the combination of high owner dependency, significant revenue volatility (21% drop), and the 'capex cliff' identified by the operational expert. The business is currently being managed for personal wealth extraction (pensions/dividends), and an earnout is essential to ensure the EBITDA remains sustainable once the owners exit and professional management is installed.","negotiation_priorities":["Normalization of working capital to account for the recent inventory spike.","Securing a long handover period to mitigate key person risk.","Price adjustment or indemnity for the fully depreciated plant and machinery.","Verification of the 'Other Creditors' balance of £123k."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Further dividend extraction prior to completion.","Refusal of key directors to sign a 24-month non-compete.","Discovery of significant undisclosed maintenance requirements for the vehicle fleet."],"key_findings":["The business has excellent liquidity (£307k cash) which should be used to fund the upfront portion of the deal.","Revenue is project-heavy (72% installation), making an earnout based on revenue stability a logical requirement.","The gap between seller expectations (£1.8M+) and fair value (£1.1M) is the primary hurdle; the earnout is the only tool to bridge this."],"narrative":"Cordell Engineering is a classic 'lifestyle' business that is financially healthy but operationally stagnant. The deal structure must balance the high cash reserves and profitability against the risks of a shrinking asset base and volatile revenue. A Conservative structure protects the buyer from the 'harvest' mentality of the current owners, ensuring that the price paid is reflective of future performance rather than historical peaks. By tying a significant portion of the consideration to a 24-month earnout, the buyer mitigates the risk of the business declining once the owners' personal relationships are removed from the sales cycle."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Cordell Engineering","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":72,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2022":{"revenue":1332473,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":695539,"gross_profit":636934,"gross_margin_percent":47.8,"administrative_expenses":525317,"operating_profit":111617,"operating_margin_percent":8.38,"depreciation_amortisation":26897,"ebitda":138514,"interest_payable":1319,"interest_coverage_ratio":84.62,"profit_before_tax":110405,"corporation_tax":19209,"effective_tax_rate_percent":17.4,"net_profit":91196,"net_margin_percent":6.84},"2023":{"revenue":1598800,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":19.99,"cost_of_sales":816112,"gross_profit":782688,"gross_margin_percent":48.95,"administrative_expenses":429450,"operating_profit":353238,"operating_margin_percent":22.09,"depreciation_amortisation":28120,"ebitda":381358,"interest_payable":959,"interest_coverage_ratio":368.34,"profit_before_tax":354021,"corporation_tax":83882,"effective_tax_rate_percent":23.7,"net_profit":270139,"net_margin_percent":16.9},"2024":{"revenue":1258568,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-21.28,"cost_of_sales":635133,"gross_profit":623435,"gross_margin_percent":49.54,"administrative_expenses":421664,"operating_profit":201771,"operating_margin_percent":16.03,"depreciation_amortisation":35386,"ebitda":237157,"interest_payable":94,"interest_coverage_ratio":2146.5,"profit_before_tax":209800,"corporation_tax":50708,"effective_tax_rate_percent":24.17,"net_profit":159092,"net_margin_percent":12.64},"2025":{"revenue":1310453,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":4.12,"cost_of_sales":676756,"gross_profit":633697,"gross_margin_percent":48.36,"administrative_expenses":380548,"operating_profit":253149,"operating_margin_percent":19.32,"depreciation_amortisation":37852,"ebitda":291001,"interest_payable":0,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":257309,"corporation_tax":51393,"effective_tax_rate_percent