,"category":"bad_debt_provision","amount":13955,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"justification":"Debtor days have ballooned from 56 to 106 days. A 5% provision on the £279,108 trade debtor balance is required to reflect increased collection risk.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":7,"case_for_inclusion":"The doubling of debtor days indicates a deteriorating credit profile and potential uncollectible accounts not currently provisioned.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may claim the debtors are blue-chip construction firms with slow but guaranteed payment cycles."},{"item":"Inventory Obsolescence Provision","category":"deferred_maintenance","amount":14654,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"justification":"Stock levels surged from zero to £293k in 24 months. A 5% obsolescence provision is prudent for digital comms hardware which has a high risk of technical depreciation.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":6,"case_for_inclusion":"Rapid stock accumulation in a technology-led sector necessitates a provision for slow-moving or obsolete hardware.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue the stock is project-specific and already committed to upcoming installations."}],"total_add_backs":3500,"total_deductions":60969,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":255532,"base":259032,"optimistic":294101},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":316501,"plus_add_backs":3500,"minus_deductions":60969,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":259032},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Sole Director","current_salary":25140,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M: Working MD (£45k-£70k)","adjustment":32360,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Revenue growth of 14% CAGR continues despite tightening liquidity.","The shift to a stock-heavy model is a permanent strategic change, not a one-off procurement error.","Staff rationalisation achieved in 2025 does not lead to operational burnout or service failure."],"sensitivity_factors":["Interest rate sensitivity on bank loans (though gearing is low).","Inventory turnover speed.","Concentration of technical knowledge in the departing owner."],"upside_scenarios":["Professionalising credit control could release £100k+ in trapped cash.","Implementing a formal inventory management system to reduce holding costs."],"downside_scenarios":["Write-down of obsolete hardware stock.","Loss of key construction contracts due to extended lead times or credit issues."]},"key_findings":["The business has excellent operational margins (31%+) but is becoming increasingly cash-inefficient.","Reported EBITDA is inflated by a significantly below-market director salary.","The balance sheet is clean (4.2% gearing) but liquidity is poor (Quick Ratio 0.71).","Gross margin volatility (51% to 84%) suggests inconsistent project costing or material procurement."],"red_flags":["Debtor days exceeding 100 days is critical for an SME.","Negative retained earnings in management accounts conflict with statutory profit figures.","Aggressive dividend extraction (73% of NP) limits reinvestment capacity."],"narrative":"The Construction Digital Comms Provider is a highly profitable but cash-hungry business. While the reported EBITDA of £316k is impressive, it is supported by an unsustainably low director salary and does not account for the risks inherent in the company's new stock-heavy model. Our adjusted Base EBITDA of £259k reflects the true cost of professional management and provides a buffer for the deteriorating quality of the debtor book. The primary value-add for an acquirer lies not in revenue growth, but in operational professionalisation—specifically credit control and inventory management—to convert high paper profits into actual cash flow."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Construction Digital Comms Provider","analysis_date":"2025-05-23","score":74,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_v