":"Directors Salaries","value":25140,"percent_of_overheads":7.81},{"category":"Motor Expenses","value":16318,"percent_of_overheads":5.07}],"cost_base_classification":"mixed"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":[],"tax_rate_consistent":false,"ebitda_latest":316501,"ebitda_trend":"growing","limitations":["Management accounts show negative retained earnings which conflict with statutory profit accumulation","Significant fluctuations in Gross Margin suggest inconsistent direct cost allocation"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":62.46,"interest_coverage_trend":"improving","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Strong. High interest coverage and low gearing (4.2%) provide significant headroom for acquisition financing."},"key_findings":["Revenue has grown at a 14% CAGR over 5 years, despite volatility in 2022 and 2024.","Operating margins have improved significantly from 12.6% in 2022 to over 31% in 2025.","The company successfully rationalised staff costs in 2025, reducing headcount while increasing revenue.","Gross margins are highly volatile (ranging 51% to 84%), suggesting project-based revenue with varying material requirements.","Dividend policy is aggressive, with £160k distributed in 2025 (73% of Net Profit).","The balance sheet has deleveraged significantly, with the gearing ratio falling to 4.2% in 2025.","Liquidity is increasingly tied to inventory, with stock levels rising 40% in the latest year."],"red_flags":["Inconsistency between management accounts (showing negative retained earnings) and statutory accounts.","Sharp decline in Quick Ratio (0.71) indicates potential cash flow pressure if inventory turnover slows.","Significant year-on-year fluctuations in Cost of Sales suggest potential accounting adjustments or lack of cost control."],"narrative":"The Construction Digital Comms Provider exhibits a robust financial profile characterised by strong earnings growth and high operational margins. Over the five-year period analysed, the company has achieved a revenue CAGR of 14%, culminating in a peak turnover of £955k in 2025. While revenue growth has been somewhat non-linear, the business has demonstrated impressive scalability; operating margins have expanded from 12.6% to 31.6%, largely due to effective overhead management and a reduction in staff costs despite higher activity levels. Earnings quality is generally high, with EBITDA tracking upwards to £316k. However, the volatility in gross margins (peaking at 84% before settling at 65%) warrants further investigation into project pricing and procurement consistency. From a balance sheet perspective, the company is exceptionally healthy with minimal long-term debt and a gearing ratio of just 4.2%. The primary concern for a buyer is the tightening liquidity; the quick ratio has dropped significantly as capital is increasingly tied up in stock and trade debtors. Furthermore, the aggressive dividend policy suggests the current owners are extracting maximum value, which may have limited historical reinvestment. Overall, the business presents a highly profitable acquisition target with significant capacity to service debt, provided the working capital cycle is stabilised post-completion."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":150,"financialPeriodId":184,"targetCompanyId":39,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":null,"prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":null,"totalCurrentAssets":null,"tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":"10653","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":"24025","bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":null,"totalCurrent