ependency on the General Manager (MB) for all operational continuity.","The £940k DLA credit balance creates a significant cash-out requirement at completion."],"narrative":"TLF Utilities is a high-performing specialist contractor with an elite financial profile for its size. The valuation is driven by a robust Adjusted EBITDA of £848k and a modern fleet that mitigates near-term Capex requirements. While the Enterprise Value is strong (Base: £2.54m), the Equity Value is tempered by the requirement to settle a £940k Director Loan Account. The primary valuation tension will be between the EBITDA-multiple approach and the high Net Asset Value; a buyer will likely pay a premium for the earnings power, but the seller may feel the business is worth more based on the 'clean' balance sheet and recent margin trajectory. The 'Zero Debtor' anomaly must be resolved before a final offer is formalized."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"TLF UTILITIES","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":68,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Minimize upfront risk and address the 'Zero Debtor' anomaly and key-man dependency through heavy deferment and performance-linked earnouts.","suitable_when":"Due diligence cannot verify the 2025 debtor position or if the General Manager (MB) refuses long-term lock-ins.","consideration":{"total_headline":2250000,"upfront_cash":1125000,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":450000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at 12 and 24 months post-completion, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":675000,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA and Key Staff Retention","earnout_period_months":36,"earnout_rationale":"Protects against the loss of the General Manager (MB) and ensures the 54.9% margin is sustainable under new ownership.","retention_escrow":225000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months following verification of 2025 tax filings and debtor collections."},"seller_obligations":{"h