 the 8% margin drop is permanent.","Extraction of 'excess' cash vs. 'operating' cash at completion."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal to provide a full indemnity for NLW compliance.","Refusal to escrow a portion of the price against the aging debtor ledger.","Any further deterioration in gross margin (>5%) between offer and completion."],"key_findings":["85% of the equity value is cash, making the deal more of a capital allocation exercise than an operational acquisition.","Operational drift is evident: headcount is up while revenue and margins are down.","The seller's price expectations are likely anchored to 2024 peaks, ignoring the 2025 downturn.","The recent £309k plant investment is the primary 'hope' factor for future growth."],"narrative":"Structuring this deal requires balancing a 'fortress' balance sheet against a weakening P&L. The primary challenge is the seller's likely expectation that they should be paid for the £4.7m cash plus a high multiple on historical (not current) earnings. The recommended Conservative structure focuses on paying for the tangible assets (Cash + NAV) upfront, while making the 'goodwill' or Enterprise Value component contingent on the business proving it can stop the current margin bleed. The tripling of debtor days is a significant red flag that must be addressed via a pound-for-pound escrow mechanism."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Building Products Manufacturer","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":72,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2018":{"revenue":2221031,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":1104462,"gross_profit":1116569,"gross_margin_percent":50.27,"administrative_expenses":710915,"operating_profit":405654,"operating_margin_percent":18.26,"depreciation_amortisation":35939,"ebitda":441593,"interest_payable":6385,"interest_coverage_ratio":63.53,"profit_before_tax":401480,"corporation_tax":74056,"effective_tax_rate_percent":18.45,"net_profit":327424,"net_margin_percent":14.74},"2019":{"r