.79,"administrative_expenses":820399,"operating_profit":423463,"operating_margin_percent":15.93,"depreciation_amortisation":54464,"ebitda":477927,"interest_payable":468,"interest_coverage_ratio":904.84,"profit_before_tax":447209,"corporation_tax":77814,"effective_tax_rate_percent":17.4,"net_profit":369395,"net_margin_percent":13.9}},"cagr":{"revenue_cagr_percent":2.63,"gross_profit_cagr_percent":1.94,"operating_profit_cagr_percent":0.61,"period_years":7},"cost_structure":{"cost_of_sales_percent_revenue":53.21,"overheads_percent_revenue":30.86,"staff_costs_percent_revenue":18.28,"director_costs_percent_revenue":4.42,"top_5_overheads":[{"category":"Staff Wages & Salaries","value":445271,"percent_of_overheads":54.27},{"category":"Directors Pension","value":117500,"percent_of_overheads":14.32},{"category":"Depreciation","value":54464,"percent_of_overheads":6.64},{"category":"Rent & Rates","value":33983,"percent_of_overheads":4.14},{"category":"Employers NI","value":32203,"percent_of_overheads":3.93}],"cost_base_classification":"mixed"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":[],"tax_rate_consistent":true,"ebitda_latest":477927,"ebitda_trend":"declining","limitations":["Amortisation not separately disclosed from depreciation in summary lines","Significant fluctuations in 'Other Direct Costs' within COS suggest accounting reclassifications"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":904.84,"interest_coverage_trend":"improving","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Exceptional. The company has negligible interest-bearing debt and a cash balance of £4.7m, allowing for significant leverage if required for acquisition."},"key_findings":["Revenue is stagnant to slightly declining, with a -2.7% contraction in the latest period and a low 7-year CAGR of 2.63%.","Gross margins are volatile, swinging from 54.9% to 46.8% in the last 12 months, indicating sensitivity to material costs or pricing pressure.","Operating profit is heavily influenced by discretionary directors' pension contributions, which fluctuated between £26k and £160k.","The balance sheet is exceptionally liquid, with £4.7m in cash representing the majority of the company's value.","A new £255k current bank loan appeared in 2025, despite high cash reserves, which requires further investigation.","Staff costs are rising as a percentage of revenue, even as turnover softens, suggesting negative operating leverage.","Interest coverage is world-class, effectively removing any immediate debt-service risk."],"red_flags":["Significant gross margin compression (8.1 percentage points) in the latest year.","Negative revenue growth in three of the last five comparable periods.","Large 'Other Direct Costs' swings in COS breakdown suggest potential inconsistencies in cost allocation."],"narrative":"The Building Products Manufacturer presents a profile of a mature, highly liquid, but growth-challenged business. From a financial performance standpoint, the company is characterized by stagnant top-line revenue and volatile profitability. While the 7-year revenue CAGR of 2.63% is positive, the recent trajectory is concerning, with year-on-year declines in 2024 and 2025. This suggests the business may be losing market share or facing a cyclical downturn in its specific manufacturing niche.\\n\\nProfitability analysis reveals significant margin compression in the latest financial year (2025), where the gross margin fell to 46.8% from a peak of 54.9% in 2024. This 810-basis point drop was the primary driver behind a 36% decline in operating profit. The cost structure is heavily weighted toward materials and staff, with administrative expenses remaining relatively fixed despite falling sales, creating negative operating leverage. However, it is noted that 'Administrative Expenses' are frequently used for tax-efficient extraction, specifically through large, variable directors' pension contributions, which masks the true underlying operational efficiency.\\n\\nEarnings quality is generally high, as net profit closely tracks operating profit with no evidence of significant exceptional items. The balance sheet is the company's greatest strength; a cash pile of £4.7m provides an immense safety buffer and suggests the business is being managed for capital preservation rather than aggressive expansion. For an acquirer, the primary value lies in this cash position and the debt-free nature of the assets. However, the lack of organic growth and the recent margin deterioration suggest that the current business model may require operational intervention or integration into a larger group to achieve economies of scale and reverse the downward earnings trend."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":139,"financialPeriodId":171,"targetCompanyId":38,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"369852","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"309709","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":"60143","computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"70000","tradeDebtors":"178427","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"192721","cashAtBank":"4728667","totalCurrentAssets":"5169815","tradeCreditors":"223653","taxationSocialSecurity":"8638","vatPayable":"44499","corporationTaxDue":"77814","bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"255000","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":"3168","amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"4682","totalCurrentLiabilities":"617454","bankLoansLongTerm":"13333","hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":null,"totalLongTermLiabilities":"13333","shareCapital":"2","retainedEarnings":"4908878","totalEquity":"4908880","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":189,"createdAt":"2026-03-26T10:08:41.809Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-26T10:08:41.809Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-03-26 10:41:29.070658	2026-04-14 08:35:35.397	share_sale
