_period_months":2,"non_compete_months":12,"non_compete_scope":"General waste services.","consultancy_arrangement":"None."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Standard fundamental warranties only.","Title to assets (fleet)."],"warranty_cap_percent":25,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Speed of execution is the priority in a competitive bid."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1000000,"expected_case":850000,"worst_case":725000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The business exhibits classic 'over-trading' symptoms: 30% revenue growth but 71% cost of sales growth and declining net assets. A Conservative structure is necessary because the current equity value is heavily inflated by a cash balance (£425k) that the owner is actively depleting via dividends. The buyer must protect against 'buying a shell' by using a completion accounts mechanism and tying a large portion of the price to the restoration of gross margins.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the 11.5% margin drop (is it fuel, disposal fees, or pricing?)","Strict 'No Leakage' provisions to protect the cash balance","Agreement on a market-rate MD salary adjustment for the EBITDA calculation","Validation of the fleet's condition and finance status"],"deal_breaker_terms":["Further dividend extraction prior to completion that takes Net Assets below the £321k floor","Refusal to accept a Gross Margin-based earnout trigger","Undisclosed environmental fines or loss of waste carrier license"],"key_findings":["Revenue growth is impressive but currently inefficient.","The seller is extracting capital faster than the business is retaining it.","The valuation gap is significant (£720k vs £1M+ expectation).","The fleet is modern (59% NBV increase) which provides some asset security."],"narrative":"Capital Waste Clearance is a high-growth but operationally 'leaky' business. The primary challenge in structuring this deal is the divergence between the impressive top-line growth and the deteriorating bottom-line efficiency. The seller likely expects a premium for the 30% growth, but the buyer is inheriting a business that is becoming more expensive to run every month. The recommended Conservative structure uses the high cash balance as a negotiation lever—offering a fair price for the equity but locking that cash inside the business through completion accounts to ensure the buyer isn't funding the acquisition of a business that has just been emptied of its liquidity."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Capital Waste Clearance","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":62,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2022":{"revenue":690804,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":213881,"gross_profit":476923,"gross_margin_percent":69.04,"administrative_expenses":235882,"operating_profit":241041,"operating_margin_percent":34.89,"depreciation_amortisation":13122,"ebitda":254163,"interest_payable":null,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":241041,"corporation_tax":47825,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.84,"net_profit":193216,"net_margin_percent":27.97},"2023":{"revenue":743173,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":7.58,"cost_of_sales":239835,"gross_profit":503338,"gross_margin_percent":67.73,"administrative_expenses":286303,"operating_profit":217035,"operating_margin_percent":29.2,"depreciation_amortisation":13086,"ebitda":230121,"interest_payable":null,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":217035,"corporation_tax":42734,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.69,"net_profit":174301,"net_margin_percent":23.45},"2024":{"revenue":969526,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":30.46,"cost_of_sales":411762,"gross_profit":557764,"gross_margin_percent":57.53,"administrative_expenses":337487,"operating_profit":220277,"operating_margin_percent":22.72,"depreciation_amortisation":20837,"ebitda":241114,"interest_payable":null,