high dividend extraction.","The company maintains a healthy liquidity position with a current ratio of 2.98, though this is down from 4.75 in 2022.","Effective tax rate increased to 25.7% in 2024, reflecting the change in UK corporation tax rates."],"red_flags":["Significant gross margin compression (11.5 percentage points in 24 months).","Negative Operating Profit CAGR (-4.4%) during a period of high revenue growth.","Substantial capital withdrawals/dividends exceeding annual net profit, leading to declining equity."],"narrative":"Capital Waste Clearance presents a profile of a rapidly growing business that is currently struggling to maintain its historical profitability levels. While the top-line trajectory is impressive—accelerating from 7.6% to 30.5% growth—this expansion has come at a significant cost to margins. The Gross Margin has eroded from 69% to 57.5%, suggesting that the company may be buying market share or is unable to pass on inflationary pressures in disposal and fuel costs to its customers. \\n\\nFrom an earnings quality perspective, EBITDA has remained remarkably flat (approx. £230k-£250k) despite the revenue surge. This indicates that the business has reached a scale where incremental revenue is being offset by a corresponding rise in the cost of delivery and administrative complexity. The cost structure is heavily influenced by motor expenses and staff costs, which are typical for the environmental services sector but require tight management to prevent further margin slippage. \\n\\nA key concern for a potential acquirer is the trend in the balance sheet. Despite generating over £530k in net profit over the last three years, total equity has fallen from £423k to £321k. This confirms a policy of aggressive dividend extraction by the current shareholders, which has limited the growth of the company's internal capital reserves. However, the business remains debt-light with a gearing ratio of 17.5% and possesses a strong current ratio of 2.98. This provides a solid foundation for a buyer to introduce debt for the acquisition. The primary focus post-acquisition must be on 'operational housekeeping'—stabilising the gross margin and leveraging the increased scale to reduce the overhead-to-revenue ratio."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":126,"financialPeriodId":156,"targetCompanyId":35,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"94925","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":null,"prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":null,"totalCurrentAssets":"425178","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":null,"totalCurrentLiabilities":"142468","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":"56149","totalLongTermLiabilities":"56149","shareCapital":null,"retainedEarnings":null,"totalEquity":"321486","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":171,"createdAt":"2026-03-26T09:55:11.468Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-26T09:55:11.468Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-03-26 11:23:38.079381	2026-03-30 16:09:38.76	share_sale
