ce","value":76427,"percent_of_overheads":15.4},{"category":"Depreciation","value":74191,"percent_of_overheads":14.95},{"category":"Staff Wages & Salaries","value":94637,"percent_of_overheads":19.07},{"category":"Other Overheads","value":46261,"percent_of_overheads":9.32}],"cost_base_classification":"predominantly_variable"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":["Significant directors pension contribution (£107k) in 2025","Other operating income (£29k) in 2021"],"tax_rate_consistent":true,"ebitda_latest":354925,"ebitda_trend":"growing","limitations":["Amortisation not separately disclosed from depreciation in all years","Detailed overhead breakdown for 2022-2023 is less granular than 2024-2025"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":13.47,"interest_coverage_trend":"improving","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Strong. The company is currently debt-free on the balance sheet (excluding HP) with high interest coverage, suggesting significant capacity for acquisition leverage."},"key_findings":["Revenue has shown a strong recovery and growth trajectory, achieving a 16.5% CAGR over the 4-year period.","Gross margins have expanded significantly from 24.5% to 36.3%, suggesting improved project selection or pricing power.","Operating leverage is evident as operating profit grew at 22.4% CAGR, outstripping revenue growth.","The 2025 administrative expenses include a £107k pension contribution which, if treated as a one-off or discretionary, would further boost underlying profitability.","The company has transitioned from a net debtor to directors to a position where directors' loans are almost entirely cleared (£3.7k remaining).","Liquidity is exceptionally strong with a current ratio of 2.90 and a cash balance of £278k.","EBITDA has grown consistently, nearly tripling from 2021 levels to £355k in 2025.","Regional concentration is high, with the Midlands accounting for 55% of revenue."],"red_flags":["High customer concentration: One client (Crawford & Company) represents 78% of the trade debtor ledger.","Debtor aging: Nearly 10% of the sales ledger is over 90 days overdue, specifically the Holloway accounts.","Volatility in staff costs: Significant jump in staff wages and headcount in 2025 may increase the fixed cost base."],"narrative":"Hickenbuild presents a robust financial profile characterized by accelerating revenue growth and significant margin expansion. Since 2021, the company has successfully scaled its top line to £2.14m while simultaneously improving its gross margin from 24.5% to 36.3%. This suggests a shift towards higher-value projects or enhanced operational efficiencies in direct cost management. Profitability is high quality, with EBITDA reaching £355k in 2025. It is important to note that 2025 earnings are arguably understated due to a discretionary £107k directors' pension contribution; adjusting for this would show even stronger underlying performance. The balance sheet has been significantly de-risked over the period, with the elimination of substantial directors' loan liabilities and the accumulation of a healthy £278k cash reserve. Gearing remains low at under 20%, primarily consisting of hire purchase for motor vehicles, leaving ample room for acquisition-related debt. The primary financial risks are external: specifically, the high concentration of revenue and receivables with a single client (Crawford & Company) and a slight deterioration in debtor aging for smaller accounts. For a buyer, the company offers a stable, profitable platform with strong cash flow generation and a clean capital structure, though the sustainability of the recent margin jump should be verified during commercial due diligence."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":106,"financialPeriodId":135,"targetCompanyId":30,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"223103","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"6762","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":"21401