dger (£160,766) is aged over 60 days, indicating significant collection risk or disputes.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":6,"case_for_inclusion":"Prudent accounting requires a provision for debt that is significantly past standard logistics payment terms.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may argue these are blue-chip clients (like Porsche) who simply have slow administrative payment processes."},{"item":"Deferred Maintenance / Fleet Catch-up","category":"deferred_maintenance","amount":65000,"justification":"Operational expert identified aging fleet units (2018/19 plates) nearing end of life; estimated annualised maintenance/replacement buffer.","recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":5,"case_for_inclusion":"The aging profile of specific vehicles necessitates higher near-term maintenance or replacement capital.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller will point to the £1.24m recent investment as evidence that the fleet is already modernized."}],"total_add_backs":-26902,"total_deductions":303266,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":1548493,"base":1575395,"optimistic":1851759},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":1878661,"plus_add_backs":-26902,"minus_deductions":276364,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":1575395},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Undisclosed Owner-Director","current_salary":0,"estimated_market_rate":77500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £5M-£10M: Working MD (£65k-£90k)","adjustment":77500,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":false,"key_assumptions":["The TNTBV contract (83.7% of revenue) remains in place and at current margin levels.","The 2025 recovery is not a one-off 'bounce' from the 2024 lows.","Other Debtors balance of £3.49m is not masking non-recoverable items."],"sensitivity_factors":["Customer Concentration: Loss of TNTBV would result in an immediate 80%+ revenue drop.","Fuel and Wage Inflation: Staff costs are 35.5% of revenue; small margin shifts significantly impact EBITDA."],"upside_scenarios":["Utilizing the £2.1m cash reserve to acquire a smaller competitor to diversify the customer base.","Improving collection on the 22% aged debt to improve cash flow."],"downside_scenarios":["TNTBV renegotiates rates downward, leveraging their position as the dominant customer.","The 'Other Debtors' balance of £3.49m is found to be unrecoverable or intercompany-related."]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA is bolstered by a recovery year, but underlying quality is threatened by extreme customer concentration.","The balance sheet contains a massive £3.49m 'Other Debtors' balance that is unexplained and exceeds the total trade debt.","2026 management accounts show a radical shift in margin (72.8% GM), suggesting a fundamental change in business model or cost misclassification."],"red_flags":["83.7% customer concentration (TNTBV).","Unexplained £3.49m 'Other Debtors' balance.","22.4% of trade debt is >60 days old.","Negative director loan balances in 2026 suggest potential extraction issues."],"narrative":"The Quality of Earnings for Logistics & Transport is moderate. While the 2025 recovery to £1.88m EBITDA is impressive, the 'Base Case' Adjusted EBITDA of £1.57m reflects the necessity of professional management and a provision for aged receivables. The most significant risk is not the earnings level itself, but the sustainability of those earnings given that nearly 84% of the business relies on a single client. Furthermore, the £3.49m in 'Other Debtors' represents a significant due diligence item; if this balance is not cash-equivalent or recoverable, the perceived strength of the balance sheet is overstated. The buyer should apply a high discount rate or a lower multiple to account for the binary risk of the TNTBV contract."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Logistics & Transport","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":74,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_ba