ty_value":6189462},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":4608030,"equity_value":5165456},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":5907731,"equity_value":6465157},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":4332336,"equity_value":4889762},"key_customer_loss_impact":"Loss of TNTBV would reduce revenue by 83.7%, likely rendering the business loss-making and reducing valuation to break-up asset value (~£2.1m fleet value).","director_replacement_impact":"Replacement cost of £77,500 reduces EBITDA by 4.9%, impacting Enterprise Value by approximately £251,875 at a 3.25x multiple."},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":7500000,"high":10000000},"seller_anchor_points":["Net Asset Value of £6.07m","2025 Revenue of £7.47m","Emotional value of 25-year blue-chip relationships","Recent £1.24m fleet investment"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. The seller is likely to anchor on the high Net Asset Value (£6.07m) and the 2025 recovery. They may expect a multiple of 5x+ on reported EBITDA (£1.88m), leading to an expectation of £9m+. A buyer will focus on the 'binary' risk of the TNTBV contract and the £3.49m 'Other Debtors' anomaly, likely offering closer to the adjusted NAV or a 3x multiple on adjusted earnings."},"key_findings":["The business is asset-rich with a strong balance sheet, but valuation is capped by extreme customer concentration.","Adjusted EBITDA of £1.57m is the most reliable earnings base after accounting for management replacement and bad debt.","The Net Asset Value (£6.07m) provides a strong floor, but the 'Other Debtors' balance of £3.49m requires urgent verification.","Cash conversion is excellent (5.7 days), indicating high operational efficiency.","The 2025 recovery is impressive but the 2022-2024 volatility suggests the business is a price-taker in its primary contract."],"red_flags":["83.7% revenue concentration in a single customer (TNTBV).","Unexplained £3.49m 'Other Debtors' balance exceeding trade debt.","22.4% of trade ledger aged over 60 days.","Negative liability entries in 2026 management accounts suggest accounting irregularities."],"narrative":"Logistics & Transport presents a classic valuation dilemma: a highly profitable, asset-rich company with a 'binary' risk profile. On an earnings basis, the business justifies an Enterprise Value of ~£5.1m. However, the Net Asset Value of £6.07m (if 'Other Debtors' are valid) actually exceeds the earnings-based valuation, suggesting the business is currently under-utilizing its asset base or that the earnings are being discounted heavily for risk. A buyer is unlikely to pay a significant premium over the adjusted Net Asset Value unless the TNTBV contract is secured long-term with 'change of control' protections. The deal structure should likely involve a 'Debt-Free/Cash-Free' adjustment and a significant earn-out tied to the retention of the primary customer."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Logistics & Transport","analysis_date":"2025-11-20","score":45,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-backed floor with binary risk mitigation via heavy earn-out.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 83.7% TNTBV concentration and the unexplained £3.49m 'Other Debtors' balance.","consideration":{"total_headline":5120000,"upfront_cash":2560000,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":560000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 12 and 24, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":2000000,"earnout_metric":"TNTBV Contract Retention & EBITDA","earnout_period_months":36,"earnout_rationale":"Protects against the 'binary' risk of losing the anchor client which represents nearly all value.","retention_escrow":500000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months pending verification of 'Other Debtors' recoverability and aged debt collection."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Logistics and transport services within the UK; specific non-solicitation of TNTBV and Porsche.","consultancy_arrangement":"Part-time consultancy for years 2 and 3 to assist with TNTBV relationship transition."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Full indemnity for any irrecoverable portion of the £3.49m 'Other Debtors' balance.","Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from negative liability entries in 2026 accounts.","Specific indemnity for HP early settlement penalties."],"warranty_cap_percent":25,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":15000,"basket":75000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":4689415,"rationale":"Necessary due to the volatility in 'Other Debtors' and the need to verify cash at the exact point of transfer."},"effective_price":{"best_case":5120000,"expected_case":4120000,"worst_case":2060000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"Hybrid approach bridging the gap between NAV and Earnings valuation.","suitable_when":"Due diligence provides reasonable comfort on the 'Other Debtors' but concentration risk remains.","consideration":{"total_headline":5700000,"upfront_cash":3705000,"upfront_percent":65,"deferred":1000000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid over 24 months in quarterly installments.","earnout_maximum":995000,"earnout_metric":"Gross Margin Maintenance & TNTBV Revenue","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Ensures the seller doesn't 'buy' revenue at the expense of margin during the transition.","retention_escrow":300000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon successful collection of 90% of the current >60 day aged debt ledger."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in the logistics sector; non-solicitation of top 5 customers.","consultancy_arrangement":"Retainer-based consultancy for 12 months."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for bad debts exceeding the £120k provision.","Indemnity for