 high cash reserves of £2.11m.","Significant customer concentration exists, with one debtor (TNTBV) representing 83.7% of the ledger.","Staff costs are the primary cost driver, representing over 35% of revenue in the latest full year.","Liquidity is exceptionally strong with a current ratio of 3.82, providing a robust operational buffer."],"red_flags":["Extreme customer concentration: 83.7% of trade debtors linked to a single entity (TNTBV).","Historical revenue instability: Significant top-line contraction between 2022 and 2024.","Aging Debtors: 22.4% of the sales ledger is aged over 60 days, indicating potential collection friction."],"narrative":"The financial performance of Logistics & Transport presents a narrative of resilience and successful recovery following a period of significant contraction. Between 2022 and 2024, the business saw a worrying 40% decline in turnover, which typically signals the loss of a major contract or a market downturn. However, the 2025 results demonstrate a robust rebound, with revenue returning to £7.47m and, more importantly, gross margins expanding to 32.9%. This margin expansion suggests that the company has successfully pivoted toward higher-value work or achieved significant operational efficiencies during the leaner years.\\n\\nFrom an earnings quality perspective, the business is fundamentally sound. EBITDA has recovered to £1.88m, and the company maintains a very conservative balance sheet. The gearing ratio of 8.7% is remarkably low for a capital-intensive transport business, and the current ratio of 3.82 indicates a surplus of liquidity. The primary financial risk is the extreme customer concentration identified in the sales ledger, where one client accounts for the vast majority of outstanding debt. Any disruption to this relationship would have a catastrophic impact on the company's ability to service its fixed cost base.\\n\\nFor an acquirer, the company offers a clean, asset-backed balance sheet with significant debt capacity. The recent investment in the fleet (tangible assets doubling since 2022) reduces the immediate need for capital expenditure post-acquisition. While the historical revenue volatility requires deep-dive due diligence into contract stickiness, the current trajectory and profitability levels make this a high-quality target within the logistics sector."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":174,"financialPeriodId":212,"targetCompanyId":44,"intangibleAssets":"0","tangibleFixedAssets":"2020896","freeholdProperty":"1368","leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":"-1512","motorVehicles":"2021039","computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"512874","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"116730","cashAtBank":"2088087","totalCurrentAssets":"2655190","tradeCreditors":"349837","taxationSocialSecurity":"246711","vatPayable":"-182245","corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"-3334282","hirePurchaseCurrent":"1082183","accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":"-49919","otherCreditors":"32999","totalCurrentLiabilities":"-1854713","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":null,"totalLongTermLiabilities":"0","shareCapital":"2","retainedEarnings":"6530797","totalEquity":"6530799","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":218,"createdAt":"2026-03-26T21:24:17.628Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-26T21:24:17.628Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-03-26 21:37:16.794239	2026-03-26 22:23:21.229	share_sale
