r a sustainable corporate entity.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller will argue that the current external accountancy support is sufficient for a business of this size and complexity."},{"item":"Bad Debt Provisioning","category":"bad_debt_provision","amount":4605,"recurrence":"recurring","year":2025,"justification":"Trade debtors have risen from £0 to £92k with a 51-day cycle. No bad debt provision is visible in the accounts. A standard 5% provision on aged debt is prudent given the rapid shift to a credit-based model.","confidence":"medium","defensibility_score":7,"case_for_inclusion":"The transition from cash-on-delivery to credit-based sales introduces inherent collection risks that are not currently reflected in the P&L.","case_for_exclusion":"The seller may claim 100% collectability based on historical payment performance of their specific client base."}],"total_add_backs":0,"total_deductions":65105,"adjusted_ebitda":{"conservative":200793,"base":200793,"optimistic":205398},"adjustment_summary":{"reported_ebitda":265898,"plus_add_backs":0,"minus_deductions":65105,"equals_adjusted_ebitda_base":200793},"director_salary_analysis":{"directors":[{"name":"Sole Director","current_salary":12000,"estimated_market_rate":57500,"benchmark_range_used":"Revenue £1M-£5M (Adjusted for £658k revenue: £45k-£70k)","adjustment":45500,"adjustment_type":"deduction"}]},"sustainability_assessment":{"sustainable_for_3_years":true,"key_assumptions":["Gross margins stabilize at 52% and do not continue the downward trend seen since 2022.","The 51-day debtor cycle does not deteriorate further, impacting cash flow.","The £90k Director's Loan Account is settled or excluded from the deal without impacting operational liquidity."],"sensitivity_factors":["Reliance on subcontractors vs. direct labour costs.","Customer concentration (not fully disclosed but implied by the debtor jump).","Ability to maintain 30% net margins while professionalizing management."],"upside_scenarios":["Automation of 'Other' sector tasks to improve the low £36k revenue-per-employee.","Leveraging the debt-free balance sheet to fund aggressive organic growth."],"downside_scenarios":["Further gross margin compression if wage inflation continues to outpace pricing.","Loss of key operational knowledge held by the sole director during transition."]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA is high but relies on an artificially low director salary of £12k.","The business has successfully scaled but is experiencing significant margin compression (67% to 52%).","The balance sheet is 'hollowed out' by a £90.6k Director's Loan Account which exceeds total Retained Earnings.","Operational efficiency is a concern with low revenue per employee and high headcount volatility."],"red_flags":["Director's Loan Account (£90,636) represents a major risk to book value and liquidity.","Gross margin has dropped 15 percentage points in 3 years.","Sudden shift in debtor days from 0 to 51 suggests a change in customer quality or power."],"narrative":"Lion Pack Entertainment Ltd shows strong top-line growth, but the 'Quality of Earnings' is impacted by owner-dependency and aggressive cost-cutting on management salaries. While the reported EBITDA of £266k is impressive for a company of this size, it is not 'transferable' in its current form. A buyer must deduct approximately £65k to account for a market-rate MD and basic financial controls. Furthermore, the significant margin compression suggests the business is losing pricing power as it scales. The most critical deal point will be the treatment of the £90k Director's Loan Account, which currently inflates the asset base but represents a liability to the buyer's future cash flow if not cleared."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Lion Pack Entertainement Ltd","analysis_date":"2025-05-23","score":72,"confidence":"medium","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":200793,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2,"multiple_justification":"A multiple of 2.0x is selected, slightly below the sector midpoint. While the company shows strong historical growth and high net margins, significant discounts are applied for micro-scale (<£1M revenue), high owner dependency (sole director), and recent dramatic slowing of revenue growth (4.4%).","premium_factors_applied":["High net profit margins (~30%)","Debt-free balance sheet","Strong interest coverage","Modern asset base (57.5% freshness)"],"discount_factors_applied":["Micro-cap scale (<£1M revenue)","High key-man dependency (sole director)","Significant revenue growth deceleration (155% to 4.4%)","Gross margin compression (15 percentage points)","High headcount volatility"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":301190,"base":401586,"optimistic":602379}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":401586,"plus_cash":49000,"minus_long_term_debt":0,"minus_director_loans":0,"minus_bad_debt_provision":46197,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":0,"equity_value":{"conservative":303993,"base":404389,"optimistic":605182}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":89069,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":-46197,"adjusted_nav":42872,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":658137,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.3,"high":0.8},"implied_ev_range":{"low":197441,"high":526510}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":300000,"equity_value_mid":405000,"equity_value_high":600000},"primary_methodology":"ebitda_multiple","cross_check_alignment":"moderate"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":441745,"equity_value":444548},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":361427,"equity_value":364230},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":501983,"equity_value":504786},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":301190,"equity_value":303993},"key_customer_loss_impact":"High - implied by the sudden jump and stagnation of trade debtors at £92k.","director_replacement_impact":-45500},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":650000,"high":1300000},"seller_anchor_points":["1x to 2x Revenue (£658k - £1.3M)","Reported EBITDA (£266k) without market-rate salary adjustments","Historical 155% growth rate"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. The seller is likely to anchor on the unadjusted EBITDA and historical growth, whereas a buyer will focus on the £65k management cost adjustment and the £90k Director Loan Account risk."},"key_findings":["The business is highly profitable but requires a £65k EBITDA adjustment to reflect market-rate management costs.","The Enterprise Value is heavily sensitive to the selected multiple due to the micro-cap nature of the entity.","The £90.6k Director's Loan Account (DLA) is a critical deal point; it currently represents the majority of the company's book value.","Revenue growth has stalled significantly in the latest year, dropping from 46% to 4.4%.","The 51-day debtor cycle and lack of bad debt provisioning suggest a potential £46k overvaluation of current assets."],"red_flags":["Director's Loan Account (£90.6k) exceeds total Retained Earnings (£89k).","Gross margin compression of 15% over 3 years indicates loss of pricing power.","Stagnant trade debtors (£92k) despite revenue growth suggests collection risks.","High headcount volatility (32 to 18) suggests operational instability."],"narrative":"Lion Pack Entertainment Ltd is a classic 'lifestyle' business that has successfully scaled but now faces a growth plateau. While the reported EBITDA of £266k is strong, the 'Quality of Earnings' adjustment for a market-rate director salary reduces this to a more realistic £201k. The valuation is primarily constrained by the company's micro-scale and high owner dependency. A multiple of 2.0x Adjusted EBITDA is appropriate given the sector and the recent slowdown in growth. The most significant hurdle in a transaction will be the 'hollow' balance sheet; the £90k Director's Loan Account must be settled or deducted from the purchase price, as it currently represents the entirety of the company's net worth. A buyer should also insist on a robust bad debt provision given the stagnation of the sales ledger."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Lion Pack Entertainement Ltd","analysis_date":"2025-05-24","score":58,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-protection focused with heavy deferment and performance-contingent earnout to mitigate growth stagnation and key-man risk.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 4.4% revenue growth plateau and the 'hollow' balance sheet caused by the Director's Loan Account.","consideration":{"total_headline":405000,"upfront_cash":162000,"upfront_percent":40,"deferred":121500,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in equal installments at month 12 and month 24 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":121500,"earnout_metric":"Adjusted EBITDA maintenance","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by 'Revenue stagnation or decline' and 'Owner/key person dependency'. Revenue growth dropped from 155% to 4.4%, and the sole director is the primary decision-maker.","retention_escrow":90636,"escrow_release_conditions":"Held specifically against the repayment or offset of the Director's Loan Account (DLA) and any undisclosed bad debts."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in the entertainment sector and solicitation of existing 18-person staff.","consultancy_arrangement":"Part-time consultancy for months 7-12 to ensure operational knowledge transfer."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Full indemnity for the £90,636 Director's Loan Account recoverability.","Specific indemnity for trade debtor collection over 90 days (£46,197).","Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from historical low director salary/dividend mix."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":2500,"basket":10000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":76139,"rationale":"Required due to high headcount volatility and the need to verify the exact status of the DLA and trade debtors at the point of transfer."},"effective_price":{"best_case":405000,"expected_case":343500,"worst_case":162000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"Standard SME structure with a 60% upfront payment and a performance-linked earnout to bridge the valuation gap.","suitable_when":"The buyer accepts the adjusted EBITDA of £201k but requires proof that the recent growth slowdown isn't a permanent decline.","consideration":{"total_headline":405000,"upfront_cash":243000,"upfront_percent":60,"deferred":81000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid at month 12 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":81000,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Floor Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by 'Revenue stagnation'. Earnout is paid if revenue remains above £625k (95% of current) to ensure the business hasn't peaked.","retention_escrow":45000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon verification of trade debtor collections and settlement of the DLA."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Entertainment sector within the UK.","consultancy_arrangement":"Available on-call for 6 months post-handover."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for DLA settlement.","Indemnity for bad debts exceeding the £4,605 provision."],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":18,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":15000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":70000,"rationale":"To adjust for the increasing working capital intensity (now 11.6% of revenue)."},"effective_price":{"best_case":405000,"expected_case":385000,"worst_case":243000}},{"name":"Competitive","strategy":"High upfront cash offer to appeal to the seller's likely high expectations, using a 'Locked Box' to provide price certainty.","suitable_when":"Multiple bidders are involved and the buyer is confident they can professionalize management quickly.","consideration":{"total_headline":450000,"upfront_cash":360000,"upfront_percent":80,"deferred":90000,"deferred_schedule":"Unconditional payment at month 12.","earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"None","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"No earnout included to make the offer more attractive, relying instead on a higher upfront and fixed deferred payments.","retention_escrow":25000,"escrow_release_conditions":"General warranty escrow for 12 months."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competitors only.","consultancy_arrangement":"None."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["DLA must be cleared prior to completion (Debt-free/Cash-free basis)."],"warranty_cap_percent":25,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":7500,"basket":20000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Provides the seller with price certainty at signing, assuming no 'leakage' occurs."},"effective_price":{"best_case":450000,"expected_case":450000,"worst_case":337500}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The 'Conservative' structure is recommended because the business's net assets are effectively zero once the £90k Director's Loan Account is removed. Furthermore, the 150% to 4% revenue growth collapse and 15% margin compression suggest a business that may have already peaked. A high upfront payment would expose the buyer to significant 'hollowed out' balance sheet risk and potential bad debt in the static £92k trade debtor balance.","negotiation_priorities":["Settlement of the £90,636 Director's Loan Account prior to or at completion.","Verification of the £92k trade debtor aging and collectability.","Agreement on the £65k EBITDA normalization for management costs.","Securing