ansition toward operational stability in 2025. While revenue growth has decelerated to 4.4% in the most recent period, the company has maintained a robust bottom-line performance, delivering a net profit of £197k on £658k turnover.\\n\\nFrom an M&A perspective, the primary concern is the consistent compression of the gross margin, which has fallen from nearly 67% to 52%. This suggests that as the company has scaled, its direct delivery costs—specifically direct labour and subcontractors—have consumed a larger portion of every pound earned. However, the business compensates for this with an exceptionally lean administrative overhead structure. The lack of external debt and the strong interest coverage ratio (2,481x) make this an ideal candidate for a leveraged acquisition, as the cash flows are more than sufficient to service debt.\\n\\nThe balance sheet is healthy, though the sudden appearance of a £90.6k Director's Loan Account as an asset in 2025 warrants investigation; if this represents cash extracted that is intended to be written off or repaid via dividends, the effective 'book value' may be lower than stated. Overall, the earnings quality is high, with Net Profit tracking Operating Profit closely, and the business demonstrates strong financial resilience. The acquisition decision should focus on whether the current 30% net margin is sustainable if further management layers are added post-acquisition."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":208,"financialPeriodId":252,"targetCompanyId":49,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"14399","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"92103","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":"49183","totalCurrentAssets":"141286","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":