ncy drivers","Interest rates on the £934k factoring facility"],"upside_scenarios":["In-sourcing drivers to capture the margin currently lost to agencies","Improving debtor days to reduce reliance on expensive factoring"],"downside_scenarios":["Further margin compression if fuel/labour costs cannot be passed to customers","Withdrawal of factoring facility due to negative working capital"]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA is heavily supported by non-core rental income (£57k).","The business is significantly under-paying directors, masking true management costs.","Operating margins have collapsed from 7% to 3.8% in four years.","The business model has shifted to high-risk agency labour, increasing variable cost exposure."],"red_flags":["Negative working capital and current ratio < 1.0 in all years.","Debtor days extended to 72 days, indicating poor credit control.","Heavy reliance on Aldermore Factoring (£934k) to fund basic operations.","Interest coverage has dropped by 70% since 2022."],"narrative":"Midas presents a challenging Quality of Earnings profile. While the reported EBITDA of £304k suggests a viable business, nearly 43% of this figure is eroded when adjusting for market-rate management salaries and removing non-core rental income. The 'true' operational EBITDA of £172k reflects a low-margin (3.1%) business that is highly sensitive to cost fluctuations. The reliance on invoice factoring and the deterioration of debtor days suggest a business under significant liquidity stress. A buyer should value the business on the adjusted £172k figure and anticipate a requirement for immediate working capital stabilization."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Midas","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":58,"confidence":"medium","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":172280,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":2,"mid":3,"high":4},"selected_multiple":2.5,"multiple_justification":"A multiple of 2.5x is selected, positioned at the lower end of the sector range. While revenue has recovered to £5.4M, the business suffers from significant margin compression (operating margin halved since 2022), high gearing, and a deteriorating interest coverage ratio. The heavy reliance on agency labor and invoice factoring increases operational risk, offsetting the stability provided by the freehold property.","premium_factors_applied":["Revenue recovery of 13% in 2025","Significant asset backing via freehold property","Scalable model due to high subcontractor usage"],"discount_factors_applied":["Operating profit CAGR of -17.68% over 3 years","High financial risk with current ratio consistently below 1.0","Significant quality of earnings adjustments (43% reduction from reported EBITDA)","High dependency on expensive invoice factoring facilities"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":344560,"base":430700,"optimistic":516840}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":430700,"plus_cash":0,"minus_long_term_debt":145000,"minus_director_loans":976,"minus_bad_debt_provision":107271,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":136876,"equity_value":{"conservative":-45563,"base":40577,"optimistic":126717}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":643000,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":-107271,"adjusted_nav":535729,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":5436463,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.3,"high":0.8},"implied_ev_range":{"low":1630939,"high":4349170}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":40577,"equity_value_mid":288153,"equity_value_high":535729},"primary_methodology":"asset_based_valuation","cross_check_alignment":"weak"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":473770,"equity_value":83647},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":387630,"equity_value":-2493},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":516840,"equity_value":126717},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":344560,"equity_value":-45563},"key_customer_loss_impact":"High. Given the thin 3.8% operating margin, the loss of a single major contract would likely render the business loss-making and unable to service its £934k factoring facility.","director_replacement_impact":"Already factored into adjusted EBITDA as a £59,979 deduction to reach market rates."},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":1500000,"high":2500000},"seller_anchor_points":["Latest revenue of £5.4M","Reported EBITDA of £304k","Net Asset Value of £643k","Emotional value of the 4-year recovery"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Extreme. The seller is likely to anchor on a 5x-7x multiple of reported EBITDA or a percentage of turnover, potentially seeking £1.5M+. However, the high debt levels, negative working capital, and necessary QoE adjustments result in a negligible equity value under an earnings-based approach. The negotiation will likely pivot to the Adjusted NAV of £535k as the only viable floor."},"key_findings":["The business is 'asset rich but cash poor', with value tied up in freehold property while operations are funded by aggressive factoring.","Adjusted EBITDA is 43% lower than reported due to non-core rental income and underpaid directors.","The equity value is severely suppressed by the requirement to normalize working capital and provide for potential bad debts.","Revenue multiples are inappropriate for this business due to the razor-thin margins and high variable cost base."],"red_flags":["Current ratio consistently below 1.0 indicates chronic liquidity stress.","Interest coverage has dropped from 18x to 5x in three years.","Debtor days have extended to 72 days, suggesting the £1.07M debtor book may be impaired.","Negative working capital of £136k requires immediate injection post-acquisition."],"narrative":"Midas presents a classic valuation dichotomy. On an earnings basis, the business is worth very little to an equity holder because the operational cash flow is almost entirely consumed by debt servicing, working capital deficits, and the cost of