nings quality is bolstered by 'Other Operating Income' (e.g., rental income), without which operating margins would be sub-3%.","Interest costs have doubled since 2022, reflecting increased debt levels or higher rates on invoice discounting facilities.","Dividend payments have increased to £78k in 2025 despite net profits being 58% lower than 2022 levels."],"red_flags":["Significant deterioration in Operating Margin from 7.0% to 3.8% over four years.","Negative working capital and current ratios consistently below 1.0 across the period.","High reliance on short-term bank loans and factoring (Aldermore) to fund operations.","Interest coverage ratio has declined by over 70% since 2022."],"narrative":"Midas exhibits the financial profile of a mature logistics business struggling with intense cost inflation and margin compression. While the top-line revenue has remained relatively stable over a four-year period (CAGR of 0.98%), the underlying profitability has eroded significantly. Operating profit in 2025 (£207k) is nearly 45% lower than the 2022 peak (£371k), despite 2025 having higher turnover. This indicates a failure to pass on direct cost increases—specifically subcontractor labour and fuel—to customers.\\n\\nThe cost structure is heavily weighted toward variable direct costs (88% of revenue), which provides some protection during downturns but limits the benefits of economies of scale during growth phases. Administrative expenses have risen as a percentage of revenue, further squeezing the bottom line. A notable concern for a buyer is the quality of earnings; the company relies on 'Other Operating Income' to maintain its slim net margins. Without this non-core income, the haulier's operational viability would be marginal.\\n\\nFrom a balance sheet perspective, the company is highly geared and suffers from chronic liquidity constraints, evidenced by a current ratio consistently below 1.0. The heavy reliance on invoice factoring and short-term bank debt suggests that cash flow is tight. While the freehold property provides some asset backing, the declining interest coverage ratio (from 18.0x to 5.0x) suggests that the business has limited capacity to service additional debt. An acquisition would likely require a significant working capital injection and a restructuring of the debt profile to stabilise the cash position."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":281,"financialPeriodId":341,"targetCompanyId":69,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"1117753.12","freeholdProperty":"799571.84","leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"30775.98","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":"110813.02","computerEquipment":"12552.6","stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"1224045.29","prepayments":"9015.96","amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"106860.76","cashAtBank":"72788.3","totalCurrentAssets":"1412710.31","tradeCreditors":"216547.84","taxationSocialSecurity":"13141.72","vatPayable":"67386.67","corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"366.52","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":"60542.06","amountsOwedToDirectors":"976.29","otherCreditors":"937485.75","totalCurrentLiabilities":"1296446.85","bankLoansLongTerm":"321634.41","hirePurchaseLongTerm":"145691.45","deferredTaxation":"74560","otherLongTermDebt":"48895.35","totalLongTermLiabilities":"590781.21","shareCapital":"50","retainedEarnings":"539186.31","totalEquity":"643235.37","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":393,"createdAt":"2026-04-16T16:19:06.003Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-16T16:19:06.003Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-04-16 16:46:28.803496	2026-04-16 18:05:41.073	share_sale
