spite high dividends.","The balance sheet was significantly altered in 2020 by a £256k freehold property acquisition funded by new bank debt.","Customer concentration is a major risk, with national housebuilders dominating the sales ledger and extending payment cycles to 130 days."],"red_flags":["Significant gross margin erosion of 600bps since 2018.","High customer concentration: Top 5 debtors represent over 40% of the ledger.","Deteriorating debtor days, reaching 129.5 days in recent reports, suggesting poor collection leverage against large contractors.","High dividend dependency may necessitate a change in capital allocation post-acquisition."],"narrative":"MSL exhibits the financial profile of a mature, highly profitable specialist contractor within the construction sector. The company has demonstrated resilience, maintaining double-digit net margins (averaging 19%) throughout the 2018-2022 period, including the COVID-19 downturn. The 2022 recovery was particularly strong, with revenue reaching a five-year high of £1.51m. However, this growth has come at the cost of margin compression; gross margins have trended downwards from 40.7% to 34.6%, likely due to the inability to fully pass on material price increases to fixed-price contracts with national housebuilders.\\n\\nFrom an earnings quality perspective, the results are clean. Operating profit closely tracks net profit, and the reliance on government grants during the pandemic was modest. The cost structure is lean, with administrative overheads well-controlled and showing positive operational gearing during the 2022 revenue surge. The primary financial risk lies in the working capital cycle. Debtor days are exceptionally high (130 days), and the sales ledger is heavily concentrated among a few large residential developers. This creates a 'squeeze' where MSL must fund its variable cost base (65% of revenue) while waiting over four months for payment.\\n\\nThe balance sheet is solid, underpinned by freehold property and a manageable gearing ratio of 33.9%. While interest coverage has declined due to the debt taken on for the property purchase, a ratio of 36x remains extremely safe. For an acquirer, the business offers stable, high-margin earnings, but success will depend on managing the working capital requirement and addressing the downward trend in gross margins through better procurement or contract indexing."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":257,"financialPeriodId":307,"targetCompanyId":60,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"287495","freeholdProperty":"246696","leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"40799","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"70027","tradeDebtors":"384404","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"7716","cashAtBank":"187563","totalCurrentAssets":"649710","tradeCreditors":"142923","taxationSocialSecurity":"63755","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":"67758","bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"5964","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"18509","totalCurrentLiabilities":"298909","bankLoansLongTerm":"154239","hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":"7196","otherLongTermDebt":"0","totalLongTermLiabilities":"161435","shareCapital":"100","retainedEarnings":"476761","totalEquity":"476861","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":341,"createdAt":"2026-04-05T17:26:53.421Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-05T17:26:53.421Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-04-05 17:33:42.989841	2026-04-15 19:47:22.208	share_sale
