d payments exceeding net profit, leading to a 38% erosion of net assets in 2025.","Interest coverage ratio dropped from 27.8x to 1.6x in three years.","Sharp increase in long-term bank debt (97% increase in 2025) during a period of declining profitability.","Net profit margin of 0.1% leaves the business vulnerable to even minor cost fluctuations."],"narrative":"PFC presents a high-risk profile for an acquirer, characterised by a sharp deterioration in financial performance over the last 24 months. While the business demonstrated healthy growth and margin expansion through 2022, the subsequent trajectory is concerning. Revenue has peaked and is now in a steady decline, while the cost base remains stubbornly fixed, leading to a near-total collapse of operating margins to 0.29% in 2025. The quality of earnings is further compromised by significant bad debt volatility and a reliance on historical government grants to bolster earlier years. From a capital structure perspective, the business is being aggressively de-capitalised by the current shareholders; the 2025 dividend payout of £250k against a net profit of only £8k has forced the company to take on substantial new debt, driving gearing from 16.6% to 52.8% in a single year. This has resulted in a critical weakening of the interest coverage ratio to 1.59x, leaving virtually no headroom for the additional debt service typically required in a leveraged acquisition. The current liquidity position, reliant on high stock levels and a widening overdraft, suggests a business struggling to manage working capital in a declining market. An acquirer would need to immediately halt dividend distributions and implement a radical overhead restructuring to restore viability."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":297,"financialPeriodId":358,"targetCompanyId":72,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"120140","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"8149","fixturesFittings":"6469","motorVehicles":"105370","computer