 specifically targets the sustainability of the 2026 gross margin recovery.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the 2026 balance sheet and current cash position.","Securing a 'stop-clause' on further dividend extractions prior to completion.","Agreement on the 'Normalised Working Capital' peg to prevent value leakage.","Validation of the subcontractor agreements and their transferability."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal to provide a 2026 trial balance or balance sheet.","Evidence that 2026 margins were driven by a single non-recurring project.","Refusal to accept a tax indemnity for historical dividend extractions."],"key_findings":["The business is debt-free and highly liquid, making it an attractive acquisition target despite governance risks.","The 2026 turnaround is impressive but requires contractual protection due to historical volatility.","High subcontractor spend (£744k) creates a variable cost base that must be managed post-acquisition.","The seller's price expectations are likely anchored to unadjusted figures, necessitating a structured bridge."],"narrative":"DHA Fire is a classic 'lifestyle' business transitioning into a high-growth service provider. While the financial metrics (debt-free, 2.8 current ratio) are excellent, the 'Quality of Earnings' is hampered by aggressive capital extraction and a lean management layer. The deal structure must bridge the gap between the seller's optimistic 2026 view and the buyer's need for margin sustainability. A Balanced approach using a Gross Margin-linked earnout provides the best compromise, ensuring the buyer doesn't overpay for a temporary spike in profitability while rewarding the seller if the turnaround is genuine."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"DHA Fire","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":68,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2023":{"revenue":1286033,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":704359,"gross_profit":581674,"gross_margin_percent":45.23,"administrative_expenses":351057,"operating_profit":230617,"operating_margin_percent":17.93,"depreciation_amortisation":5433,"ebitda":236050,"interest_payable":2889,"interest_coverage_ratio":79.83,"profit_before_tax":228030,"corporation_tax":43352,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.01,"net_profit":184678,"net_margin_percent":14.36},"2024":{"revenue":1350878,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":5.04,"cost_of_sales":818196,"gross_profit":532682,"gross_margin_percent":39.43,"administrative_expenses":395673,"operating_profit":137009,"operating_margin_percent":10.14,"depreciation_amortisation":4970,"ebitda":141979,"interest_payable":0,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":138356,"corporation_tax":32649,"effective_tax_rate_percent":23.6,"net_profit":105707,"net_margin_percent":7.83},"2025":{"revenue":1522045,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":12.67,"cost_of_sales":1077645,"gross_profit":444400,"gross_margin_percent":29.2,"administrative_expenses":421901,"operating_profit":22499,"operating_margin_percent":1.48,"depreciation_amortisation":8303,"ebitda":30802,"interest_payable":0,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":23234,"corporation_tax":5117,"effective_tax_rate_percent":22.02,"net_profit":18117,"net_margin_percent":1.19},"2026":{"revenue":1790145.7,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":17.61,"cost_of_sales":904006.24,"gross_profit":886139.46,"gross_margin_percent":49.5,"administrative_expenses":371138.04,"operating_profit":515001.42,"operating_margin_percent":28.77,"depreciation_amortisation":null,"ebitda":null,"interest_payable":null,"interest_coverage_ratio":null,"profit_before_tax":515001.42,"corporation_tax":null,"net_profit":515001.42,"net_margin_percent":28.77}},"cagr":{"revenue_cagr_percent":11.65,"gross_profit_cagr_percent":15.06,"operating_profit_cagr_percent":30.7,"period_years":3},"cost_structure":{"cost_of_sales_percent_revenue":50.5,"overheads_percent_revenue":20.73,"staff_costs_percent_revenue":6.92,"director_costs_percent_revenue":1.8,"top_5_overheads":[{"category":"Staff Wages & Salaries","value":96214.57,"percent_of_overheads":25.92},{"category":"Travel & Subsistence","value":74522.67,"percent_of_overheads":20.08},{"category":"Other Overheads","value":36212.33,"percent_of_overheads":9.76},{"category":"Directors Salaries","value":32193.12,"percent_of_overheads":8.67},{"category":"Insurance","value":23120.29,"percent_of_overheads":6.23}],"cost_base_classification":"predominantly_variable"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":[{"year":2025,"description":"Profit on sale of tangible assets","amount":1325}],"tax_rate_consistent":false,"ebitda_latest":null,"ebitda_trend":"stable","limitations":["Depreciation not provided in 2026 management accounts","Tax and Net Profit for 2026 are pre-tax/estimated","Balance sheet data missing for 2026"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":null,"interest_coverage_trend":"improving","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"High. The company has eliminated interest-bearing debt and shows strong operating cash flow potential in 2026."},"key_findings":["Revenue shows accelerating growth, with a 17.6% increase in the latest period (2026).","Gross margins have been highly volatile, dropping to 29.2% in 2025 before a sharp recovery to 49.5% in 2026.","Operating efficiency improved dramatically in 2026, with the operating margin reaching a record 28.8%.","Travel and subsistence costs are a disproportionately high overhead, consistently representing ~20% of administrative expenses.","The company maintains a debt-free balance sheet as of the latest statutory filings (2025).","Dividend policy is aggressive, with payments in 2024 and 2025 exceeding net profits, leading to a depletion of retained earnings.","The shift toward subcontractor costs in 2026 (£744k) suggests a flexible, scalable labour model."],"red_flags":["Significant margin compression observed in 2025 (Net Margin 1.2%) indicates high sensitivity to direct cost fluctuations.","Aggressive dividend extraction has historically weakened the capital base (Net Assets fell 33.8% in 2025).","Lack of 2026 Balance Sheet data prevents verification of current liquidity or year-end cash position."],"narrative":"DHA Fire presents a financial profile characterized by strong top-line momentum and a recent, significant recovery in profitability. Between 2023 and 2025, the company faced severe margin pressure, with net margins collapsing from 14.4% to just 1.2% as cost of sales outpaced revenue growth. However, the 2026 management accounts indicate a successful turnaround or a shift in project mix, with gross margins rebounding to 49.5% and operating profit reaching £515k. This volatility suggests that while the business is capable of high performance, it is sensitive to direct cost inputs or pricing strategy. From an M&A perspective, the company is attractive due to its debt-free status and lean fixed-cost base, which is predominantly variable through the use of subcontractors. The primary concern for a buyer is the historical dividend policy; the directors have consistently extracted more than the annual net profit, which has eroded the net asset position. Future acquisition debt could be comfortably serviced by the 2026 earnings level, but a buyer must ensure that the recent margin expansion is sustainable and not the result of a single high-margin contract. The high travel and subsistence spend (£74k-£98k) suggests an opportunity for operational tightening post-acquisition."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":300,"financialPeriodId":363,"targetCompanyId":74,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":null,"prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":null,"totalCurrentAssets":null,"tradeCr