ounts suggest weak financial controls.","Owner Dependency: Directors perform all key functions; no middle management exists."],"narrative":"Holdfast Engineering is a high-performing but high-risk acquisition target. From a financial perspective, its 21% operating margin and 55% CAGR are exceptional for the Facilities Management sector. However, the valuation is heavily tempered by the fact that nearly 85% of revenue is tied to just three clients. A 'Base Case' Equity Value of £1.2M is recommended, representing a 2.5x multiple on adjusted EBITDA plus surplus cash. To protect the buyer, any deal should be structured with a significant portion of the consideration (40-50%) tied to an earn-out based on the retention of the top three clients over 24 months. The forensic due diligence must prioritize the 'negative debtor' entries and the recoverability of the £461k trade debtor balance."}	\N	74	medium	9081	{"promptTokenCount":8019,"candidatesTokenCount":1781,"totalTokenCount":9800}	19	{financial,qoe,sector,risk,operational}	2026-03-24 21:11:09.457807	2026-03-24 21:11:50.591
