"],"narrative":"Air Conditioning Sales Uk Limited presents a valuation paradox. On an earnings basis (EBITDA multiple), the business has no equity value because its long-term debt and recommended bad debt provisions far outweigh its capitalized earnings. However, the company maintains a strong balance sheet on paper with £186k in net assets. A rational buyer would not pay for the earnings of this business given the 'key-man' risk and debt load; instead, the valuation must be anchored to the Adjusted Net Asset Value. The primary risk to this valuation is the quality of the trade debtors; if the £238k balance is not fully collectible, the value of the business evaporates. Any deal should be structured as an asset purchase or include a heavy debt-settlement mechanism at completion."}	\N	72	medium	27436	{"promptTokenCount":7182,"candidatesTokenCount":1711,"totalTokenCount":8893}	30	{financial,qoe,sector,risk,operational}	2026-04-03 16:56:08.761534	2026-04-03 16:57:39.46
