abilities and the accumulation of a healthy £278k cash reserve. Gearing remains low at under 20%, primarily consisting of hire purchase for motor vehicles, leaving ample room for acquisition-related debt. The primary financial risks are external: specifically, the high concentration of revenue and receivables with a single client (Crawford & Company) and a slight deterioration in debtor aging for smaller accounts. For a buyer, the company offers a stable, profitable platform with strong cash flow generation and a clean capital structure, though the sustainability of the recent margin jump should be verified during commercial due diligence."}	\N	82	high	17289	{"promptTokenCount":36829,"candidatesTokenCount":2696,"totalTokenCount":39525}	17	\N	2026-03-25 16:34:12.845651	2026-03-25 16:34:30.619
