ue, requiring an immediate £19.6k provision."],"narrative":"Hickenbuild is a high-performing but concentrated construction firm. Its valuation of ~£1.05m (Base Equity Value) reflects a balance between its impressive 36% gross margins and the systemic risk of its reliance on a single major client. While the company has successfully scaled and modernized its fleet, the high working capital intensity and owner-dependency necessitate a conservative multiple (2.5x). A deal structure involving a 40-50% earn-out linked to the retention of Crawford & Company would be the most likely path to a successful transaction, protecting the buyer while allowing the seller to achieve their higher price expectations if the business remains stable post-sale."}	\N	72	high	19128	{"promptTokenCount":9193,"candidatesTokenCount":1717,"totalTokenCount":12112}	17	{financial,qoe,sector,risk,operational}	2026-03-25 16:34:13.006682	2026-03-25 16:35:14.426
