rer presents a rare profile of extreme financial stability coupled with a softening top-line. The company is essentially a 'cash box', holding 4.7m in liquid reserves against a turnover of 2.6m, with virtually no debt. This provides a massive safety buffer for an acquirer. However, the trajectory is concerning: revenue has declined for two years, and 2025 saw a sharp compression in gross margins (from 54.9% to 46.8%), suggesting either pricing pressure or unrecovered input cost inflation. Asset quality is high following a recent 300k+ investment in plant. The primary risk is the 'unknown' regarding customer concentration and the reason for the recent sales decline. If the revenue drop is due to a deliberate exit from low-margin work, the outlook is positive; if it is due to market share loss, the valuation must be adjusted. Further due diligence should focus exclusively on the sales pipeline and gross margin recovery plan."}	\N	\N	\N	10954	{"promptTokenCount":23773,"candidatesTokenCount":1597,"totalTokenCount":25370}	22	{data_quality}	2026-03-26 10:09:18.056915	2026-03-26 10:09:29.057
