t Company 1 presents a mixed profile that requires careful valuation adjustment. The primary concern is the significant and sustained contraction in profitability. Between 2020 and 2023, the Gross Margin fell from 40% to 29%, and Operating Profit dropped by nearly 38% in absolute terms. This suggests the company has been unable to pass on cost increases to customers or has shifted toward lower-margin wholesale work. Revenue growth is essentially flat, with the 2023 turnover still below 2020 levels, indicating a lack of organic momentum. \\n\\nHowever, the business demonstrates excellent fiscal discipline in other areas. Management has aggressively reduced administrative expenses and deleveraged the balance sheet. The interest coverage ratio of 34.3x is exceptional, and the reduction in gearing from 35.6% to 13.1% provides significant 'headroom' for an acquirer to introduce acquisition debt. Liquidity is also robust, with a quick ratio now exceeding 1.0, meaning the business is not reliant on inventory liquidation to meet short-term obligations. \\n\\nThe earnings quality is generally high, with net profit tracking operating profit closely and a consistent tax treatment. The 2025 management accounts suggest that while margins have stabilised at the 'new normal' of 29%, they are not yet recovering to historical highs. For a buyer, the investment case rests on whether the margin compression can be reversed through post-acquisition synergies or if the current 6% operating margin represents the ceiling for this business model. The sharp decline in tangible assets since 2020 also warrants specific legal and operational due diligence to ensure core infrastructure was not divested to prop up cash flow."}	\N	58	high	13483	{"promptTokenCount":12637,"candidatesTokenCount":2131,"totalTokenCount":14768}	1	\N	2026-03-27 11:41:44.660997	2026-03-27 11:41:58.598
