n the current cash position?","Can you provide a breakdown of the 131k trade debtors to assess collectability and age?"],"comparable_context":"In the UK cleaning sector, gross margins of 55% are upper-quartile, but successful firms typically convert this to 5-10% net profit. IHateCleaning's failure to reach break-even at 1.5m revenue suggests an inefficient overhead structure or unsustainable debt servicing costs compared to sector peers.","executive_summary":"DO NOT PROCEED. IHateCleaning presents a high-risk profile that does not meet the criteria for further investigation. While the company has successfully scaled revenue from 292k to 1.5m over five years and maintains a modern, high-quality vehicle fleet, it has failed to translate this growth into sustainable profit. The business returned to a significant net loss in 2025 (94,293) after a marginal profit in 2024. The balance sheet is structurally compromised, characterized by a 1.06m accumulated deficit and total reliance on 855k in shareholder support to remain operational. Most critically, cash reserves have depleted by nearly 80% to just 10,926, leaving the company unable to service its 174k in bank debt or daily operations without further external capital. The combination of negative cash flow, high gearing, and inconsistent earnings makes this an unattractive acquisition target at this stage."}	\N	\N	\N	11175	{"promptTokenCount":42673,"candidatesTokenCount":1649,"totalTokenCount":44322}	28	{data_quality}	2026-03-30 12:07:43.38157	2026-03-30 12:07:54.601
