argins of 2-5%, whereas ARSL is currently at -5.2%.","executive_summary":"The recommendation for ARSL is DO NOT PROCEED. The company is exhibiting classic signs of financial distress, characterized by a sharp swing from profitability to a significant net loss and a critical depletion of cash reserves. Revenue has begun to contract following the exit of a non-core business line, but administrative expenses have not been reduced quickly enough to compensate, leading to negative operating margins. The balance sheet is under severe pressure; the current ratio of 0.8 indicates that the company cannot meet its short-term obligations with its current assets. Furthermore, the business is increasingly reliant on director loans and hire purchase agreements to fund operations. Without an immediate and radical turnaround in trading performance or a significant capital injection, the business faces a high risk of insolvency. The lack of granular data on customers and staff further limits the ability to identify any hidden value that might justify the high turnaround risk."}	\N	\N	\N	9999	{"promptTokenCount":8786,"candidatesTokenCount":1526,"totalTokenCount":10312}	15	{data_quality}	2026-04-03 18:51:43.450553	2026-04-03 18:51:53.497
