ovide a minimum 6-month handover.","Significant undisclosed liabilities related to the Ashford hub expansion."],"key_findings":["The business is highly profitable but optimized for owner extraction (£700k+ p.a.).","The £59m order book is a rare and powerful value driver for an SME.","Operational leverage is a concern as admin costs are outstripping revenue growth.","The 2025 bad debt provision of £94k indicates a need for tighter credit controls."],"narrative":"Window Company (2) is a classic 'lifestyle' business that has grown into a substantial enterprise. The deal structure must bridge the gap between the owners' high personal income and the business's statutory reality. By using an earnout tied to the conversion of the massive order book, the buyer can safely pay a premium multiple while ensuring the 'brain trust' (the directors) remains motivated to transition the business effectively. The primary focus of the structure is ensuring that the 31% gross margins are not just historical artifacts but are embedded in the future contracted work."}	\N	74	high	157630	{"promptTokenCount":7197,"candidatesTokenCount":2402,"totalTokenCount":9599}	22	{valuation,risk,operational,qoe}	2026-04-09 18:29:45.711548	2026-04-09 18:33:15.304
