ative":"Printing Company (C) presents a classic 'lifestyle' business profile where true earnings are masked by aggressive profit extraction. While the reported EBITDA of £348k is modest, the normalization of £243k in pension contributions reveals an underlying EBITDA capacity in excess of £500k. The business has shown impressive resilience by growing operating profit 63% despite a 10% revenue decline, proving the success of its shift toward a higher-margin, lower-material-cost model. However, the buyer must account for the 'institutionalization' cost—specifically hiring a management layer to replace the heavily involved directors and addressing the stagnation in machinery investment. The adjusted EBITDA of £520k (Base Case) is defensible, but the valuation should reflect the risks associated with high customer concentration and the aging asset base."}	\N	62	high	13311	{"promptTokenCount":47342,"candidatesTokenCount":2078,"totalTokenCount":49420}	22	{financial,operational}	2026-04-11 18:33:28.093236	2026-04-11 18:34:05.718
