t at month 12.","earnout_maximum":80000,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Revenue stagnation/decline (Risk expert). Ensures the customer base remains stable during the transition.","retention_escrow":40000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Standard 12-month release."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":2,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition.","consultancy_arrangement":"None."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Intercompany balance settlement"],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Provides price certainty to the seller, suitable for a competitive process, using the 2025 balance sheet as the box date."},"effective_price":{"best_case":800000,"expected_case":760000,"worst_case":640000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The 73% collapse in operating profit and the heavy reliance on £102k of intercompany add-backs make this a high-risk acquisition. The Conservative structure protects the buyer by making a significant portion of the price contingent on the business actually proving it can generate the 'Adjusted EBITDA' without parent company support.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification and elimination of the £142k intercompany debt.","Validation of the £102k management charge as a discretionary add-back.","Securing a cash-free/debt-free completion mechanism to capture the £411k cash balance.","Addressing the 15.5% rise in direct labour costs."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Failure to waive or capitalize the £142,211 intercompany liability.","Any further erosion of gross margin below 30% prior to completion.","Refusal of a completion accounts mechanism."],"key_findings":["Equity value is artificially high due to a £411k cash balance, but trading performance is declining.","The business is a 'c