D. Midas is currently exhibiting classic signs of a 'profitable' business facing a liquidity crisis. While the company reports net profits and holds valuable freehold property, its balance sheet is severely over-leveraged with short-term debt. Revenue has entered a downward trajectory, falling 12.8% in the last year, and net margins have more than halved since 2022. Most critically, the cash position has collapsed to just 29,507 against current liabilities of 1.15m. Unless the acquisition is viewed as a distressed asset play for the freehold property, the operational business carries excessive financial risk."}	\N	\N	\N	14472	{"promptTokenCount":16847,"candidatesTokenCount":1496,"totalTokenCount":18343}	15	{data_quality}	2026-04-16 16:18:26.149088	2026-04-16 16:18:40.668
