hy was there a zero corporation tax charge in 2021 despite a reported profit before tax of 2.8m?"],"comparable_context":"A 40% gross margin is upper-quartile for UK manufacturing, but the 10% annual revenue decline contrasts sharply with a sector that has seen modest inflationary growth. Most healthy peers would show a cash conversion ratio of 80%+, which this target is failing to meet.","executive_summary":"Acme Manufacturing Ltd presents as a technically proficient business with high-quality assets and disciplined pricing, yet it is in a clear state of contraction. While the 40% gross margin and 2.0 current ratio are superficially attractive, the underlying trends are concerning. Revenue has declined from 28.5m to 21.2m over four years, and management accounts for 2024 suggest this trend is continuing. Most critically, there is a major disconnect between the 1.9m annual net profit and the declining cash balance, suggesting that value is being aggressively extracted from the business rather than reinvested. Without sales ledger data to rule out customer churn or bad debt, and given the failure of the primary financial health dimensions (Earnings and Cash), this target does not warrant further investment of due diligence resources."}	\N	\N	\N	11455	{"promptTokenCount":29728,"candidatesTokenCount":1634,"totalTokenCount":31362}	1	{data_quality}	2026-04-16 18:30:29.733719	2026-04-16 18:30:41.235
